1
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,196
<i>This is the Asgardian</i>

2
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:30,740
<i>refugee vessel</i> Statesman.

3
00:00:33,492 --> 00:00:34,785
<i>We are under assault.</i>

4
00:00:34,869 --> 00:00:36,954
<i>I repeat,
we are under assault.</i>

5
00:00:37,121 --> 00:00:40,666
<i>The engines are dead,
life support failing.</i>

6
00:00:40,833 --> 00:00:43,794
<i>Requesting aid
from any vessel within range.</i>

7
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:46,964
<i>We are 22 jump points
out of Asgard.</i>

8
00:00:47,965 --> 00:00:50,593
<i>Our crew is made up
of Asgardian families.</i>

9
00:00:50,676 --> 00:00:52,178
<i>We have
very few soldiers here.</i>

10
00:00:52,345 --> 00:00:54,222
<i>This is not a war craft.</i>

11
00:00:54,305 --> 00:00:56,307
<i>I repeat,
this is not a war craft.</i>

12
00:01:09,779 --> 00:01:12,782
Hear me and rejoice.

13
00:01:16,577 --> 00:01:18,829
You have had the privilege

14
00:01:18,913 --> 00:01:21,582
of being saved
by the Great Titan.

15
00:01:24,543 --> 00:01:26,754
You may think
this is suffering.

16
00:01:27,964 --> 00:01:28,965
No.

17
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:32,343
It is salvation.

18
00:01:36,222 --> 00:01:39,934
Universal scales
tip toward balance

19
00:01:40,017 --> 00:01:41,769
because of your sacrifice.

20
00:01:43,396 --> 00:01:44,814
Smile.

21
00:01:46,065 --> 00:01:48,150
For even in death,

22
00:01:48,234 --> 00:01:50,695
you have become
Children of Thanos.

23
00:02:06,127 --> 00:02:08,170
I know what it's like to lose.

24
00:02:10,339 --> 00:02:13,301
To feel so desperately
that you're right...

25
00:02:14,051 --> 00:02:16,804
yet to fail, nonetheless.

26
00:02:24,895 --> 00:02:26,522
It's frightening.

27
00:02:27,857 --> 00:02:29,817
Turns the legs to jelly.

28
00:02:31,944 --> 00:02:34,071
But I ask you, to what end?

29
00:02:35,489 --> 00:02:38,075
Dread it, run from it...

30
00:02:39,118 --> 00:02:41,662
destiny arrives all the same.

31
00:02:42,872 --> 00:02:44,707
And now, it's here.

32
00:02:45,291 --> 00:02:47,126
Or should I say...

33
00:02:48,461 --> 00:02:49,962
I am.

34
00:02:55,426 --> 00:02:56,761
You talk too much.

35
00:02:58,054 --> 00:02:59,513
The Tesseract.

36
00:02:59,889 --> 00:03:02,016
Or your brother's head.

37
00:03:06,687 --> 00:03:09,065
I assume you have
a preference.

38
00:03:10,316 --> 00:03:11,609
Oh, I do.

39
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:15,071
Kill away.

40
00:03:30,336 --> 00:03:31,462
All right, stop!

41
00:03:35,007 --> 00:03:36,967
We don't have the Tesseract.

42
00:03:37,134 --> 00:03:38,969
It was destroyed on Asgard.

43
00:03:49,772 --> 00:03:52,650
You really are
the worst brother.

44
00:03:57,696 --> 00:03:59,573
I assure you, brother...

45
00:03:59,740 --> 00:04:01,700
the sun will shine
on us again.

46
00:04:03,661 --> 00:04:06,664
Your optimism is misplaced,
Asgardian.

47
00:04:06,997 --> 00:04:10,793
Well, for one thing,
I'm not Asgardian.

48
00:04:11,127 --> 00:04:12,169
And for another...

49
00:04:14,588 --> 00:04:15,756
we have a Hulk.

50
00:04:27,143 --> 00:04:29,854
Let him have his fun.

51
00:05:22,156 --> 00:05:23,616
AIlfathers...

52
00:05:25,493 --> 00:05:28,746
let the dark magic flow
through me one last...

53
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:30,664
time.

54
00:05:45,471 --> 00:05:46,972
That was a mistake.

55
00:05:52,853 --> 00:05:54,522
No!

56
00:06:03,656 --> 00:06:06,283
You're going to die for that.

57
00:06:09,411 --> 00:06:10,663
Shh.

58
00:06:17,545 --> 00:06:19,296
My humble personage...

59
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:23,008
bows before your grandeur.

60
00:06:26,303 --> 00:06:29,515
No other being
has ever had the might...

61
00:06:29,932 --> 00:06:31,600
nay, the nobility...

62
00:06:31,976 --> 00:06:36,689
to wield not one,
but two Infinity Stones.

63
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:44,572
The universe lies
within your grasp.

64
00:06:44,572 --> 00:07:14,572
<b>Subtitle | www.movieddl.me</b>

65
00:07:23,819 --> 00:07:26,572
There are two more stones
on Earth.

66
00:07:28,032 --> 00:07:31,535
Find them, my children,
and bring them to me on Titan.

67
00:07:31,827 --> 00:07:33,245
Father, we will not fail you.

68
00:07:33,412 --> 00:07:34,913
If I might interject.

69
00:07:36,081 --> 00:07:39,376
If you're going to Earth,
you might want a guide.

70
00:07:40,294 --> 00:07:42,880
I do have a bit of experience
in that arena.

71
00:07:42,963 --> 00:07:45,382
If you consider
failure experience.

72
00:07:45,466 --> 00:07:48,218
I consider
experience experience.

73
00:07:49,428 --> 00:07:50,929
Almighty Thanos...

74
00:07:51,221 --> 00:07:55,893
I, Loki, prince of Asgard...

75
00:07:59,688 --> 00:08:00,898
Odinson...

76
00:08:04,818 --> 00:08:06,737
the rightful king
of Jotunheim...

77
00:08:07,363 --> 00:08:09,239
god of mischief...

78
00:08:10,115 --> 00:08:11,617
do hereby pledge to you...

79
00:08:13,035 --> 00:08:16,914
my undying fidelity.

80
00:08:27,466 --> 00:08:28,967
Undying?

81
00:08:32,763 --> 00:08:35,432
You should choose your words
more carefully.

82
00:08:56,954 --> 00:08:57,955
You...

83
00:08:59,081 --> 00:09:00,666
will never be...

84
00:09:03,377 --> 00:09:04,461
a god.

85
00:09:14,805 --> 00:09:15,806
No!

86
00:09:30,779 --> 00:09:33,282
No resurrections this time.

87
00:09:56,889 --> 00:09:59,057
No. Loki.

88
00:10:37,846 --> 00:10:40,849
<i>Seriously,
you don't have any money?</i>

89
00:10:40,933 --> 00:10:43,977
Attachment to the material is
detachment from the spiritual.

90
00:10:44,144 --> 00:10:45,437
I'll tell the guys
at the deli.

91
00:10:45,604 --> 00:10:47,481
Maybe they'll make you
a metaphysical ham on rye.

92
00:10:47,648 --> 00:10:49,483
Oh. Wait, wait, wait.
I think I have 200.

93
00:10:49,650 --> 00:10:50,651
Dollars?

94
00:10:50,818 --> 00:10:52,152
- Rupees.
- Which is?

95
00:10:52,736 --> 00:10:54,154
Uh, buck and a half.

96
00:10:54,321 --> 00:10:55,531
What do you want?

97
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:58,325
I wouldn't say no
to a tuna melt.

98
00:11:10,796 --> 00:11:12,756
Thanos is coming.

99
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:14,550
He's coming.

100
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,138
Who?

101
00:11:28,939 --> 00:11:30,107
Slow down, slow down.
I'll spell it out for you.

102
00:11:30,190 --> 00:11:31,191
You're totally rambling.

103
00:11:31,275 --> 00:11:32,317
- No, I'm not.
- You lost me.

104
00:11:32,401 --> 00:11:33,527
Look, you know how
you're having a dream,

105
00:11:33,610 --> 00:11:34,736
and in the dream
you gotta pee.

106
00:11:34,903 --> 00:11:35,904
- Yeah.
- Okay.

107
00:11:36,071 --> 00:11:37,197
And then you're like,
"Oh, my God.

108
00:11:37,281 --> 00:11:38,448
"There's no bathrooms.
What am I gonna do?

109
00:11:38,532 --> 00:11:39,533
- "Oh, someone's watching."
- Right.

110
00:11:39,616 --> 00:11:40,617
"Oh, I'm gonna
go in my pants."

111
00:11:40,701 --> 00:11:41,785
And then you wake up
and in real life

112
00:11:41,869 --> 00:11:42,911
you actually have to pee.

113
00:11:42,995 --> 00:11:43,996
- Yes.
- Yeah.

114
00:11:44,079 --> 00:11:45,205
- Okay.
- Everybody has that.

115
00:11:45,372 --> 00:11:47,082
Right, that's the point
I'm trying to make.

116
00:11:47,416 --> 00:11:51,420
Apropos of that, last night
I dreamt we had a kid.

117
00:11:52,004 --> 00:11:53,213
It was so real.

118
00:11:53,589 --> 00:11:54,923
We named him
after your eccentric uncle.

119
00:11:55,007 --> 00:11:56,008
Uh, what was his name?

120
00:11:56,174 --> 00:11:58,427
- Right.
- Morgan! Morgan.

121
00:11:58,594 --> 00:12:00,220
- So you woke up...
- Naturally.

122
00:12:00,387 --> 00:12:01,972
...and thought that we were...

123
00:12:02,139 --> 00:12:03,223
- Expecting.
- Yeah.

124
00:12:03,307 --> 00:12:04,349
- Yes?
- No.

125
00:12:04,433 --> 00:12:05,809
I had a dream about it.
It was so real.

126
00:12:05,976 --> 00:12:07,311
If you wanted to have a kid...

127
00:12:07,978 --> 00:12:09,396
you wouldn't have done that.

128
00:12:10,063 --> 00:12:12,024
I'm glad you brought this up,
'cause it's nothing.

129
00:12:12,107 --> 00:12:13,525
It's just a housing unit
for nanoparticles.

130
00:12:13,692 --> 00:12:15,110
You're not helping
your case, okay?

131
00:12:15,193 --> 00:12:16,320
No, this is detachable.
It's not a...

132
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:17,946
You don't need that.

133
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,364
I know, I had the surgery.

134
00:12:19,448 --> 00:12:20,490
I'm just
trying to protect us...

135
00:12:20,574 --> 00:12:22,326
and future usses
and that's it.

136
00:12:22,492 --> 00:12:24,077
Just in case there's a monster
in the closet.

137
00:12:24,161 --> 00:12:26,079
- Instead of, you know...
- Shirts.

138
00:12:27,748 --> 00:12:29,207
You know me so well.

139
00:12:29,291 --> 00:12:32,002
- God.
- You finish all my sentences.

140
00:12:32,544 --> 00:12:34,421
You should have shirts
in your closet.

141
00:12:34,796 --> 00:12:35,797
Yeah.

142
00:12:36,632 --> 00:12:38,342
You know what there should be?
No more surprises.

143
00:12:38,508 --> 00:12:39,676
We're gonna have
a nice dinner tonight.

144
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:41,970
Show off this Harry Winston.

145
00:12:42,054 --> 00:12:44,389
Right? And we should have
no more surprises. Ever.

146
00:12:44,556 --> 00:12:45,599
I should promise you.

147
00:12:45,766 --> 00:12:47,059
- Yes.
- I will.

148
00:12:49,519 --> 00:12:50,562
Thank you.

149
00:12:50,646 --> 00:12:51,813
Tony Stark.

150
00:12:51,980 --> 00:12:54,983
I'm Doctor Stephen Strange.
I need you to come with me.

151
00:12:56,985 --> 00:12:59,571
Oh, uh, congratulations
on the wedding, by the way.

152
00:12:59,738 --> 00:13:01,615
I'm sorry, you giving out
tickets to something?

153
00:13:01,698 --> 00:13:03,116
We need your help.

154
00:13:03,909 --> 00:13:05,494
It's not overselling it
to say that

155
00:13:05,577 --> 00:13:07,120
the fate of the universe
is at stake.

156
00:13:07,204 --> 00:13:08,747
And who's "we"?

157
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:11,500
Hey, Tony.

158
00:13:11,583 --> 00:13:12,709
Bruce.

159
00:13:12,876 --> 00:13:14,503
- Pepper.
- Hi.

160
00:13:17,506 --> 00:13:19,132
- Oh.
- You okay?

161
00:13:20,926 --> 00:13:23,095
At the dawn
of the universe,

162
00:13:23,178 --> 00:13:25,138
there was nothing. Then...

163
00:13:25,514 --> 00:13:26,807
Boom.

164
00:13:27,349 --> 00:13:30,686
The Big Bang sent
six elemental crystals...

165
00:13:30,852 --> 00:13:33,689
hurtling across
the virgin universe.

166
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:36,274
These Infinity Stones

167
00:13:36,358 --> 00:13:39,277
each control an essential
aspect of existence.

168
00:13:40,237 --> 00:13:41,405
Space.

169
00:13:42,531 --> 00:13:43,699
Reality.

170
00:13:45,325 --> 00:13:46,493
Power.

171
00:13:47,703 --> 00:13:48,870
Soul.

172
00:13:49,997 --> 00:13:51,164
Mind.

173
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:54,334
And Time.

174
00:14:03,927 --> 00:14:05,178
Tell me his name again.

175
00:14:05,262 --> 00:14:06,471
Thanos.

176
00:14:06,638 --> 00:14:07,931
He's a plague, Tony.

177
00:14:08,015 --> 00:14:09,891
He invades planets.
He takes what he wants.

178
00:14:10,058 --> 00:14:12,269
He wipes out
half the population.

179
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:14,062
He sent Loki.

180
00:14:14,688 --> 00:14:17,607
The attack on New York,
that's him.

181
00:14:18,191 --> 00:14:19,317
This is it.

182
00:14:20,485 --> 00:14:21,486
What's our timeline?

183
00:14:21,570 --> 00:14:23,780
No telling. He has
the Power and Space Stones.

184
00:14:23,947 --> 00:14:24,948
That already makes him

185
00:14:25,032 --> 00:14:26,575
the strongest creature
in the whole universe.

186
00:14:26,742 --> 00:14:30,078
If he gets his hands
on all six stones, Tony...

187
00:14:30,162 --> 00:14:31,246
He could destroy life

188
00:14:31,329 --> 00:14:33,331
on a scale
hitherto undreamt of.

189
00:14:33,415 --> 00:14:35,375
Did you seriously just say
"hitherto undreamt of'?

190
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,586
Are you seriously leaning
on the Cauldron of the Cosmos?

191
00:14:37,753 --> 00:14:39,254
Is that what it is?

192
00:14:42,007 --> 00:14:43,925
I'm going to allow that.

193
00:14:46,136 --> 00:14:47,596
If Thanos needs all six,
why don't we just

194
00:14:47,679 --> 00:14:49,139
stick this one down
a garbage disposal?

195
00:14:49,222 --> 00:14:50,223
No can do.

196
00:14:50,390 --> 00:14:53,101
We swore an oath to protect
the Time Stone with our lives.

197
00:14:53,268 --> 00:14:54,394
And I swore off dairy...

198
00:14:54,478 --> 00:14:57,064
but then Ben & Jerry's named
a flavor after me.

199
00:14:57,147 --> 00:14:58,607
- Stark Raving Hazelnuts.
- Not bad.

200
00:14:58,774 --> 00:15:00,150
A bit chalky.

201
00:15:00,317 --> 00:15:01,860
A Hunk of Hulk of
Burning Fudge is our favorite.

202
00:15:02,027 --> 00:15:03,153
- That's a thing?
- Whatever.

203
00:15:03,236 --> 00:15:04,404
Point is, things change.

204
00:15:04,571 --> 00:15:07,407
Our oath to protect
the Time Stone cannot change.

205
00:15:07,491 --> 00:15:09,618
And this stone may be the best
chance we have against Thanos.

206
00:15:09,701 --> 00:15:10,702
Yeah, so conversely,

207
00:15:10,786 --> 00:15:12,662
it may also be
his best chance against us.

208
00:15:12,746 --> 00:15:14,206
Well, if we don't do our jobs.

209
00:15:14,289 --> 00:15:15,290
What is your job exactly?

210
00:15:15,373 --> 00:15:17,000
Besides making
balloon animals.

211
00:15:18,126 --> 00:15:20,754
Protecting your reality,
douche bag.

212
00:15:20,837 --> 00:15:23,340
Okay, guys. Could we table
this discussion right now?

213
00:15:23,507 --> 00:15:25,383
The fact is
we have this stone.

214
00:15:25,467 --> 00:15:26,760
We know where it is.

215
00:15:27,135 --> 00:15:29,471
Vision is out there somewhere
with the Mind Stone...

216
00:15:29,638 --> 00:15:31,348
and we have to find him now.

217
00:15:32,140 --> 00:15:33,558
Yeah, that's the thing.

218
00:15:33,642 --> 00:15:34,643
What do you mean?

219
00:15:34,768 --> 00:15:36,978
Two weeks ago, Vision turned
off his transponder.

220
00:15:37,062 --> 00:15:38,188
He's offline.

221
00:15:38,271 --> 00:15:39,523
- What?
- Yeah.

222
00:15:39,689 --> 00:15:41,691
Tony, you lost
another super-bot?

223
00:15:41,775 --> 00:15:44,027
I didn't lose him. He's more
than that. He's evolving.

224
00:15:44,194 --> 00:15:45,654
Who could find Vision then?

225
00:15:48,657 --> 00:15:49,658
Shit.

226
00:15:50,325 --> 00:15:51,326
Probably Steve Rogers.

227
00:15:51,493 --> 00:15:52,661
Oh, great.

228
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:54,329
Maybe.

229
00:15:54,955 --> 00:15:55,956
But...

230
00:15:59,417 --> 00:16:00,544
Call him.

231
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:02,587
It's not that easy.

232
00:16:03,672 --> 00:16:05,549
God, we haven't caught up
in a spell, have we?

233
00:16:05,632 --> 00:16:06,633
No.

234
00:16:06,716 --> 00:16:08,385
The Avengers broke up.
We're toast.

235
00:16:09,010 --> 00:16:10,095
Broke up?

236
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:13,974
Like a band?
Like... Like the Beatles?

237
00:16:14,057 --> 00:16:15,976
Cap and I fell out hard.

238
00:16:16,977 --> 00:16:18,145
We're not on speaking terms.

239
00:16:19,604 --> 00:16:22,107
Tony, listen to me.

240
00:16:23,191 --> 00:16:24,526
Thor's gone.

241
00:16:26,236 --> 00:16:27,404
Thanos is coming.

242
00:16:27,487 --> 00:16:29,114
It doesn't matter
who you're talking to or not.

243
00:16:46,381 --> 00:16:47,382
Flip phone.

244
00:17:08,486 --> 00:17:09,696
Say, Doc, you wouldn't
happen to be

245
00:17:09,779 --> 00:17:10,947
moving your hair, would ya?

246
00:17:11,907 --> 00:17:14,117
Not at the moment, no.

247
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:48,652
You okay?

248
00:17:49,778 --> 00:17:50,779
- Help him!
- Banner!

249
00:17:50,946 --> 00:17:52,530
- Wong! Look alive!
- Go, go! We got it!

250
00:17:52,697 --> 00:17:53,740
Friday, what am I looking at?

251
00:17:53,823 --> 00:17:55,158
<i>Not sure.
I'm working on it.</i>

252
00:17:55,325 --> 00:17:57,369
Hey! You might wanna
put that Time Stone

253
00:17:57,452 --> 00:17:58,662
in your back pocket, Doc!

254
00:17:58,828 --> 00:18:00,038
Might wanna use it.

255
00:18:27,482 --> 00:18:29,776
Ned, hey. I need you
to cause a distraction.

256
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:31,236
Holy shit.

257
00:18:31,611 --> 00:18:33,154
We're all gonna die!

258
00:18:33,238 --> 00:18:34,447
There's a spaceship!

259
00:18:34,614 --> 00:18:36,324
- What's going on?
- Oh, my God!

260
00:18:44,874 --> 00:18:45,959
What's the matter
with you kids?

261
00:18:46,042 --> 00:18:47,836
You never seen
a spaceship before?

262
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:02,434
Friday, evac anyone
south of 43rd Street.

263
00:19:02,517 --> 00:19:03,518
Notify first responders.

264
00:19:03,685 --> 00:19:04,853
<i>Will do.</i>

265
00:19:33,214 --> 00:19:36,134
Hear me and rejoice.

266
00:19:37,510 --> 00:19:38,970
You are about to die

267
00:19:39,054 --> 00:19:41,097
at the hands
of the Children of Thanos.

268
00:19:41,181 --> 00:19:43,725
Be thankful...

269
00:19:43,892 --> 00:19:46,436
that your meaningless lives
are now contributing...

270
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:49,564
I'm sorry,
Earth is closed today.

271
00:19:49,731 --> 00:19:52,442
You better pack it up
and get outta here.

272
00:19:52,609 --> 00:19:53,735
Stonekeeper.

273
00:19:54,694 --> 00:19:57,030
Does this chattering animal
speak for you?

274
00:19:57,113 --> 00:19:58,907
Certainly not.
I speak for myself.

275
00:19:59,366 --> 00:20:01,785
You're trespassing in
this city and on this planet.

276
00:20:02,786 --> 00:20:04,245
He means get lost, Squidward.

277
00:20:04,412 --> 00:20:05,580
He exhausts me.

278
00:20:05,663 --> 00:20:07,707
Bring me the stone.

279
00:20:09,334 --> 00:20:10,794
Banner, you want a piece?

280
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:13,171
Mmm, no, not really.

281
00:20:13,254 --> 00:20:14,547
But when do I ever get
what I want?

282
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:15,715
That's right.

283
00:20:16,424 --> 00:20:17,634
Okay. Push!

284
00:20:17,801 --> 00:20:19,260
It's been a while.

285
00:20:19,427 --> 00:20:20,929
It's gonna be good
to have you, buddy.

286
00:20:21,096 --> 00:20:22,097
Okay. Shh.

287
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,933
Let me just... I need to
concentrate here for a second.

288
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:26,351
Come on, come on, man.

289
00:20:26,434 --> 00:20:28,728
God!

290
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:31,106
Where's your guy?

291
00:20:32,524 --> 00:20:33,983
I don't know. We've sorta
been having a thing.

292
00:20:34,067 --> 00:20:35,110
- It's no time for a thing.
- I know.

293
00:20:35,276 --> 00:20:36,736
That's the thing right there.
Let's go.

294
00:20:43,952 --> 00:20:45,120
Dude, you're embarrassing me
in front of the wizards.

295
00:20:45,286 --> 00:20:47,205
Tony, I'm sorry.
Either I can't or he won't.

296
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:48,289
It's okay.

297
00:20:48,373 --> 00:20:50,750
Hey, stand down.
Keep an eye on him. Thank you.

298
00:20:50,917 --> 00:20:52,252
- I have him.
- Damn it.

299
00:21:19,946 --> 00:21:21,114
Where'd that come from?

300
00:21:21,281 --> 00:21:22,323
<i>It's nanotech.</i>

301
00:21:22,407 --> 00:21:23,450
<i>You like it?
A little something I...</i>

302
00:21:27,203 --> 00:21:29,497
Doctor Banner, if the rest
of your green friend

303
00:21:29,581 --> 00:21:30,707
won't be joining us...

304
00:21:40,383 --> 00:21:41,634
<i>Gotta get that stone
outta here, now.</i>

305
00:21:41,718 --> 00:21:43,136
It stays with me.

306
00:21:43,303 --> 00:21:44,637
Exactly. Bye.

307
00:21:53,980 --> 00:21:55,190
Tony, you okay?

308
00:21:55,356 --> 00:21:57,317
- How we doing? Good? Bad?
- <i>Really, really good.</i>

309
00:21:57,400 --> 00:21:58,526
<i>Really good.
Do you plan on helping out?</i>

310
00:21:58,693 --> 00:21:59,986
I'm trying. He won't come out.

311
00:22:01,863 --> 00:22:02,947
<i>Hammer.</i>

312
00:22:10,705 --> 00:22:13,583
Come on, Hulk!
What are you doing to me?

313
00:22:13,750 --> 00:22:15,877
Come out! Come out! Come out!

314
00:22:16,044 --> 00:22:18,254
No!

315
00:22:22,133 --> 00:22:23,927
What do you mean, "no"?

316
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:31,309
Hey, man.
What's up, Mr. Stark?

317
00:22:31,476 --> 00:22:34,270
- <i>Kid, where'd you come from?</i>
- A field trip to MoMA.

318
00:22:36,314 --> 00:22:37,774
Uh, what is this guy's
problem, Mr. Stark?

319
00:22:38,691 --> 00:22:39,943
Uh, he's from space.

320
00:22:40,026 --> 00:22:41,986
He came here to steal
a necklace from a wizard.

321
00:23:08,638 --> 00:23:10,473
Your powers are quaint.

322
00:23:10,557 --> 00:23:12,308
You must be popular
with children.

323
00:23:15,270 --> 00:23:17,063
It's a simple spell
but quite unbreakable.

324
00:23:17,230 --> 00:23:19,190
Then I'll take it
off your corpse.

325
00:23:32,245 --> 00:23:37,417
You'll find removing a
dead man's spell troublesome.

326
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:39,168
You'll only wish
you were dead.

327
00:23:49,429 --> 00:23:50,430
No!

328
00:23:54,601 --> 00:23:56,102
<i>Kid,
that's the wizard. Get on it.</i>

329
00:23:56,269 --> 00:23:57,812
On it!

330
00:24:05,236 --> 00:24:06,613
Not cool.

331
00:24:10,867 --> 00:24:11,868
Gotcha!

332
00:24:13,369 --> 00:24:14,621
Wait!

333
00:24:22,045 --> 00:24:24,672
Uh, Mr. Stark,
I'm being beamed up.

334
00:24:24,756 --> 00:24:26,174
<i>Hang on, kid.</i>

335
00:24:41,856 --> 00:24:43,232
Oh!

336
00:24:45,026 --> 00:24:46,027
Ugh.

337
00:24:46,110 --> 00:24:47,862
<i>Wong, you're invited
to my wedding.</i>

338
00:24:55,411 --> 00:24:56,537
Give me a little juice,
Friday.

339
00:25:05,463 --> 00:25:06,881
Unlock 17:A.

340
00:25:19,894 --> 00:25:21,479
Pete, you gotta let go.
I'm gonna catch you.

341
00:25:21,562 --> 00:25:23,731
But you said
save the wizard!

342
00:25:24,148 --> 00:25:25,149
I can't breathe.

343
00:25:26,442 --> 00:25:28,111
We're too high up.
You're running out of air.

344
00:25:29,070 --> 00:25:31,322
Yeah. That makes sense.

345
00:25:48,506 --> 00:25:50,508
Mr. Stark, it smells
like a new car in here!

346
00:25:50,675 --> 00:25:51,718
<i>Happy trails, kid.</i>

347
00:25:51,801 --> 00:25:53,219
- <i>Friday, send him home.</i>
<i>- Yep.</i>

348
00:25:54,178 --> 00:25:55,638
Oh, come on!

349
00:26:04,063 --> 00:26:06,065
<i>Boss, incoming call
from Miss Potts.</i>

350
00:26:06,232 --> 00:26:07,233
<i>Tony? Oh, my God.</i>

351
00:26:07,316 --> 00:26:08,317
<i>Are you all right?
What's going on?</i>

352
00:26:08,484 --> 00:26:09,777
<i>Yeah, I'm fine.
I just think</i>

353
00:26:09,861 --> 00:26:11,154
<i>we might have to push
our 8:</i><i>30 res.</i>

354
00:26:11,237 --> 00:26:12,321
<i>Why?</i>

355
00:26:12,405 --> 00:26:13,906
<i>Just 'cause
I'll probably</i>

356
00:26:13,990 --> 00:26:15,408
<i>not make it back for a while.</i>

357
00:26:16,492 --> 00:26:17,744
<i>Tell me
you're not on that ship.</i>

358
00:26:17,827 --> 00:26:18,828
Yeah.

359
00:26:18,911 --> 00:26:20,246
<i>God, no, please tell me
you're not on the ship.</i>

360
00:26:20,413 --> 00:26:21,998
Honey, I'm sorry.

361
00:26:22,165 --> 00:26:23,332
I'm sorry,
I don't know what to say.

362
00:26:23,416 --> 00:26:24,667
<i>Come back here, Tony.
I swear to God.</i>

363
00:26:24,834 --> 00:26:26,919
- Pep.
- <i>Come back here right now.</i>

364
00:26:27,044 --> 00:26:28,045
<i>Come back.</i>

365
00:26:28,212 --> 00:26:30,131
<i>Boss,
we're losing her.</i>

366
00:26:30,798 --> 00:26:32,341
<i>I'm going too.</i>

367
00:26:41,434 --> 00:26:42,685
Oh, my God!

368
00:26:47,148 --> 00:26:49,108
I shoulda stayed on the bus.

369
00:27:03,456 --> 00:27:04,832
Where you going?

370
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:06,501
The Time Stone's been taken.

371
00:27:06,667 --> 00:27:08,586
The Sanctum remains unguarded.

372
00:27:09,212 --> 00:27:10,671
What will you do?

373
00:27:11,464 --> 00:27:13,132
I'm gonna make a call.

374
00:27:53,422 --> 00:27:54,590
Sing it, Drax!

375
00:28:07,186 --> 00:28:08,563
Why are we doing this again?

376
00:28:08,729 --> 00:28:10,356
It's a distress signal,
Rocket.

377
00:28:10,439 --> 00:28:11,440
Someone could be dying.

378
00:28:11,607 --> 00:28:13,693
I get that,
but why are we doing it?

379
00:28:13,860 --> 00:28:15,653
'Cause we're nice.

380
00:28:15,820 --> 00:28:16,821
And maybe whoever it is

381
00:28:16,904 --> 00:28:18,573
will give us a little
cheddar cheese for our effort.

382
00:28:18,739 --> 00:28:21,075
- Which isn't the point.
- Which isn't the point.

383
00:28:21,242 --> 00:28:22,952
I mean,
if he doesn't pony up...

384
00:28:23,119 --> 00:28:24,161
We take his ship.

385
00:28:24,328 --> 00:28:25,997
- Exactly!
- Bingo!

386
00:28:26,080 --> 00:28:27,206
All right!

387
00:28:30,376 --> 00:28:31,836
We are arriving.

388
00:28:32,253 --> 00:28:33,254
All right, Guardians,

389
00:28:33,337 --> 00:28:34,463
don't forget
this might be dangerous...

390
00:28:34,630 --> 00:28:36,924
so let's put on
our mean faces.

391
00:28:42,179 --> 00:28:43,723
Groot, put that
thing away, now.

392
00:28:43,806 --> 00:28:44,807
I don't wanna tell you again.

393
00:28:44,891 --> 00:28:46,017
Groot.

394
00:28:46,183 --> 00:28:47,310
I am Groot!

395
00:28:47,393 --> 00:28:48,394
- Whoa!
- Language!

396
00:28:48,519 --> 00:28:49,854
- Hey!
- Wow.

397
00:28:50,021 --> 00:28:51,689
You got some
acorns on you, kid.

398
00:28:51,856 --> 00:28:53,399
Ever since
you got a little sap,

399
00:28:53,482 --> 00:28:54,483
you're a total d-hole.

400
00:28:55,443 --> 00:28:58,696
Now, keep it up, and I'm gonna
smash that thing to pieces.

401
00:29:05,620 --> 00:29:07,163
What happened?

402
00:29:11,208 --> 00:29:12,543
Oh, my God.

403
00:29:18,132 --> 00:29:19,884
Looks like
we're not getting paid.

404
00:29:22,136 --> 00:29:24,096
Wipers! Wipers!

405
00:29:24,263 --> 00:29:25,556
Get it off.

406
00:29:32,229 --> 00:29:34,982
How the hell
is this dude still alive?

407
00:29:35,149 --> 00:29:36,943
He is not a dude.

408
00:29:37,109 --> 00:29:38,653
You're a dude.

409
00:29:38,986 --> 00:29:42,031
This... This is a man.

410
00:29:42,406 --> 00:29:45,159
A handsome, muscular man.

411
00:29:45,326 --> 00:29:46,327
I'm muscular.

412
00:29:46,410 --> 00:29:47,411
But who are you
kidding, Quill?

413
00:29:47,495 --> 00:29:48,871
You're one sandwich
away from fat.

414
00:29:48,955 --> 00:29:49,956
Yeah, right.

415
00:29:50,039 --> 00:29:51,540
It's true, Quill.
You have put on weight.

416
00:29:51,624 --> 00:29:52,959
What?

417
00:29:54,919 --> 00:29:56,754
Gamora, do you think I'm...

418
00:29:59,048 --> 00:30:02,635
He is anxious, angry.

419
00:30:02,802 --> 00:30:05,680
He feels
tremendous loss and guilt.

420
00:30:06,555 --> 00:30:09,308
It's like a pirate had a baby
with an angel.

421
00:30:09,392 --> 00:30:10,476
Wow.

422
00:30:10,559 --> 00:30:12,436
This is a real wake-up call
for me. Okay.

423
00:30:12,603 --> 00:30:15,314
I'm gonna get a Bowflex.
I'm gonna commit.

424
00:30:15,481 --> 00:30:16,482
I'm gonna get some dumbbells.

425
00:30:16,607 --> 00:30:17,942
You know you can't
eat dumbbells, right?

426
00:30:18,109 --> 00:30:19,318
It's like his muscles

427
00:30:19,402 --> 00:30:21,320
are made
of Cotati metal fibers.

428
00:30:21,487 --> 00:30:23,197
Stop massaging his muscles.

429
00:30:24,991 --> 00:30:25,992
Wake him up.

430
00:30:29,078 --> 00:30:30,079
Wake.

431
00:30:47,680 --> 00:30:49,932
Who the hell are you guys?

432
00:30:52,727 --> 00:30:56,355
The entire time I knew Thanos,
he only ever had one goal.

433
00:30:56,522 --> 00:30:58,232
To bring balance
to the universe

434
00:30:58,315 --> 00:31:00,484
by wiping out
half of all life.

435
00:31:01,402 --> 00:31:03,612
He used to kill people
planet by planet,

436
00:31:03,696 --> 00:31:05,072
massacre by massacre.

437
00:31:05,364 --> 00:31:06,741
Including my own.

438
00:31:06,907 --> 00:31:08,492
If he gets
all six Infinity Stones...

439
00:31:08,659 --> 00:31:10,870
he can do it with the snap
of his fingers like this.

440
00:31:11,871 --> 00:31:14,457
You seem to know
a great deal about Thanos.

441
00:31:14,623 --> 00:31:18,419
Gamora
is the daughter of Thanos.

442
00:31:22,465 --> 00:31:24,550
Your father killed my brother.

443
00:31:24,884 --> 00:31:26,093
Oh, boy.

444
00:31:26,260 --> 00:31:27,928
Stepfather, technically.

445
00:31:28,095 --> 00:31:30,014
And she hates him
as much as you do.

446
00:31:33,726 --> 00:31:35,269
Families can be tough.

447
00:31:35,436 --> 00:31:36,771
Before my father died,

448
00:31:36,854 --> 00:31:38,606
he told me
that I had a half-sister...

449
00:31:38,773 --> 00:31:41,025
that he imprisoned in Hel.

450
00:31:41,192 --> 00:31:44,153
And then she returned home
and stabbed me in the eye.

451
00:31:44,320 --> 00:31:45,613
So I had to kill her.

452
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:47,823
That's life though,
isn't it, I guess.

453
00:31:47,907 --> 00:31:49,158
Goes round and round and...

454
00:31:49,992 --> 00:31:50,993
I feel your pain.

455
00:31:51,160 --> 00:31:53,454
I feel your pain as well,
because...

456
00:31:53,621 --> 00:31:54,789
I mean,
it's not a competition,

457
00:31:54,872 --> 00:31:55,998
but I've been through a lot.

458
00:31:56,165 --> 00:31:57,833
My father killed my mother.

459
00:31:58,000 --> 00:31:59,126
And then I had to kill
my father.

460
00:31:59,210 --> 00:32:00,711
That was hard.

461
00:32:00,878 --> 00:32:03,756
Probably even harder
than having to kill a sister.

462
00:32:04,298 --> 00:32:07,176
Plus, I came out with
both my eyes, which was...

463
00:32:07,343 --> 00:32:09,053
I need a hammer, not a spoon.

464
00:32:10,888 --> 00:32:13,974
How do I open this thing?
Is there some sort of, uh...

465
00:32:14,517 --> 00:32:17,061
A four-digit code, maybe?
Maybe a birth date.

466
00:32:17,144 --> 00:32:20,523
- Uh, what are you doing?
- Taking your pod.

467
00:32:21,982 --> 00:32:23,025
No, you're not.

468
00:32:25,152 --> 00:32:29,031
You will not be taking
our pod today, sir.

469
00:32:29,532 --> 00:32:32,910
Uh... Quill, are you making
your voice deeper?

470
00:32:34,829 --> 00:32:36,455
- No.
- You are.

471
00:32:36,622 --> 00:32:39,333
You're imitating the god-man.
It's weird.

472
00:32:39,500 --> 00:32:40,668
No, I'm not.

473
00:32:40,835 --> 00:32:42,878
- He just did it again!
- This is my voice.

474
00:32:49,051 --> 00:32:50,052
Are you mocking me?

475
00:32:50,511 --> 00:32:53,430
- Are you mocking me?
- Stop it. You did it again.

476
00:32:53,931 --> 00:32:54,932
He's trying to copy me.

477
00:32:55,015 --> 00:32:56,016
I need you to stop doing that.

478
00:32:56,183 --> 00:32:57,810
- Enough!
- He's doing it first.

479
00:32:57,977 --> 00:32:59,353
We need to stop Thanos.

480
00:32:59,520 --> 00:33:01,063
Which means
we need to find out

481
00:33:01,147 --> 00:33:02,148
where he's going next.

482
00:33:02,314 --> 00:33:03,566
Knowhere.

483
00:33:03,732 --> 00:33:05,401
He must be going somewhere.

484
00:33:05,568 --> 00:33:07,570
No, no. Knowhere?

485
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:10,406
It's a place.
We've been there. It sucks.

486
00:33:10,573 --> 00:33:12,992
- Excuse me, that's our food.
- Not anymore.

487
00:33:13,409 --> 00:33:16,579
Thor, why would he
go to Knowhere?

488
00:33:16,745 --> 00:33:17,913
Because for years...

489
00:33:18,080 --> 00:33:20,249
the Reality Stone's been
safely stored there

490
00:33:20,332 --> 00:33:21,750
with a man
called the Collector.

491
00:33:21,917 --> 00:33:23,502
If it's with the
Collector, then it's not safe.

492
00:33:23,669 --> 00:33:25,462
Only an idiot
would give that man a stone.

493
00:33:25,546 --> 00:33:26,922
- Or a genius.
- How do you know...

494
00:33:27,089 --> 00:33:29,633
he's not going
for one of the other stones?

495
00:33:29,800 --> 00:33:32,178
There are six stones
out there.

496
00:33:32,344 --> 00:33:34,555
Thanos already has
the Power Stone...

497
00:33:34,722 --> 00:33:38,017
because he stole it last week
when he decimated Xandar.

498
00:33:38,475 --> 00:33:40,519
He stole the Space Stone
from me...

499
00:33:40,686 --> 00:33:43,355
when he destroyed my ship and
slaughtered half my people.

500
00:33:43,522 --> 00:33:45,149
The Time and Mind Stones
are safe on Earth.

501
00:33:45,232 --> 00:33:46,233
They're with the Avengers.

502
00:33:46,567 --> 00:33:48,819
- The Avengers?
- Earth's mightiest heroes.

503
00:33:48,986 --> 00:33:50,112
Like Kevin Bacon?

504
00:33:50,279 --> 00:33:51,572
He may be on the team.
I don't know.

505
00:33:51,655 --> 00:33:52,656
I haven't been there
in a while.

506
00:33:52,823 --> 00:33:55,034
As for the Soul Stone, well,
no one's ever seen that.

507
00:33:55,201 --> 00:33:56,827
No one even knows where it is.

508
00:33:56,994 --> 00:33:58,746
Therefore Thanos can't get it.

509
00:33:58,829 --> 00:34:00,289
Therefore he's going
to Knowhere.

510
00:34:00,456 --> 00:34:02,875
Hence he'll be getting
the Reality Stone.

511
00:34:03,042 --> 00:34:04,084
You're welcome.

512
00:34:04,251 --> 00:34:05,461
Then we have to go
to Knowhere now.

513
00:34:05,628 --> 00:34:09,298
Wrong. Where we have to go
is Nidavellir.

514
00:34:09,757 --> 00:34:11,592
- That's a made-up word.
- All words are made up.

515
00:34:11,759 --> 00:34:14,845
Nidavellir is real? Seriously?

516
00:34:15,012 --> 00:34:16,639
That place is a legend.

517
00:34:16,805 --> 00:34:18,224
They make the most powerful,
horrific weapons

518
00:34:18,307 --> 00:34:20,351
to ever torment the universe.

519
00:34:20,517 --> 00:34:22,561
I would very much like
to go there, please.

520
00:34:22,728 --> 00:34:23,729
The rabbit is correct

521
00:34:23,812 --> 00:34:24,813
and clearly the smartest
among you.

522
00:34:24,939 --> 00:34:25,981
Rabbit?

523
00:34:26,148 --> 00:34:28,400
Only Eitri the <i>Dwarf</i> can
make me the weapon I need.

524
00:34:28,567 --> 00:34:29,777
I assume
you're the captain, sir.

525
00:34:29,944 --> 00:34:30,945
You're very perceptive.

526
00:34:31,111 --> 00:34:32,321
You seem like a noble leader.

527
00:34:32,404 --> 00:34:33,989
Will you join me
on my quest to Nidavellir?

528
00:34:34,156 --> 00:34:36,951
Let me just ask the captain.
Oh, wait a second, it's me!

529
00:34:37,117 --> 00:34:38,869
- Yeah. I'll go.
- Wonderful!

530
00:34:39,036 --> 00:34:40,162
Uh, except for that
I'm the captain.

531
00:34:40,246 --> 00:34:41,247
Quiet.

532
00:34:41,330 --> 00:34:42,915
- That's my backpack.
- Go sit down.

533
00:34:43,082 --> 00:34:44,708
Look, this is my ship.

534
00:34:44,875 --> 00:34:46,627
And I'm not goin' to...

535
00:34:47,628 --> 00:34:49,713
Wait, what kinda weapon
are we talkin' about here?

536
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:51,131
The Thanos-killing kind.

537
00:34:51,966 --> 00:34:53,467
Don't you think that we should
all have a weapon like that?

538
00:34:53,634 --> 00:34:55,678
No. You simply lack
the strength to wield them.

539
00:34:55,844 --> 00:34:56,929
Your bodies would crumble

540
00:34:57,012 --> 00:34:58,180
as your minds collapsed
into madness.

541
00:34:58,347 --> 00:35:00,266
Is it weird that I wanna do it
even more now?

542
00:35:00,432 --> 00:35:01,600
Mmm, a little bit, yeah.

543
00:35:01,767 --> 00:35:03,018
If we don't go to Knowhere

544
00:35:03,102 --> 00:35:04,687
and Thanos retrieves
another stone...

545
00:35:04,853 --> 00:35:06,397
he'll be too powerful to stop.

546
00:35:06,563 --> 00:35:08,732
- He already is.
- I got it figured out.

547
00:35:08,899 --> 00:35:10,609
We got two ships

548
00:35:10,693 --> 00:35:12,069
and a large assortment
of morons.

549
00:35:12,236 --> 00:35:15,489
So me and Groot will go
with the pirate angel here.

550
00:35:15,656 --> 00:35:16,824
And the morons
will go to Knowhere

551
00:35:16,907 --> 00:35:18,492
to try to stop Thanos.

552
00:35:18,659 --> 00:35:20,577
- Cool? Cool.
- So cool.

553
00:35:20,744 --> 00:35:22,037
For the record...

554
00:35:22,788 --> 00:35:24,123
I know that
you're going with him

555
00:35:24,206 --> 00:35:25,291
because it's where
Thanos isn't.

556
00:35:25,457 --> 00:35:26,959
You know, you really shouldn't

557
00:35:27,042 --> 00:35:29,169
talk that way
to your captain, Quill.

558
00:35:30,129 --> 00:35:31,463
Come on, Groot.

559
00:35:32,006 --> 00:35:34,717
Put that game down.
You'll rot your brain.

560
00:35:38,429 --> 00:35:41,265
I bid you farewell
and good luck, morons.

561
00:35:41,432 --> 00:35:42,558
Bye.

562
00:35:57,323 --> 00:35:58,449
Vis?

563
00:35:58,907 --> 00:36:00,826
Is it the stone again?

564
00:36:00,993 --> 00:36:02,619
It's as if
it's speaking to me.

565
00:36:03,245 --> 00:36:04,955
What does it say?

566
00:36:05,873 --> 00:36:08,208
I don't... I don't know,
but something.

567
00:36:09,793 --> 00:36:11,670
Hey.

568
00:36:21,513 --> 00:36:24,016
Tell me what you feel.

569
00:36:31,023 --> 00:36:33,734
I just feel you.

570
00:36:41,909 --> 00:36:43,827
So there's a 10:00 a.m.
to Glasgow...

571
00:36:43,994 --> 00:36:45,996
which would give us more time
together before you went back.

572
00:36:46,163 --> 00:36:47,623
What if
I miss that train?

573
00:36:47,790 --> 00:36:48,791
There's an 11 :00.

574
00:36:48,957 --> 00:36:51,377
What if I missed
all the trains?

575
00:36:52,753 --> 00:36:54,463
What if this time
I didn't go back?

576
00:36:54,630 --> 00:36:55,964
But you gave Stark your word.

577
00:36:56,131 --> 00:36:57,299
I'd rather give it to you.

578
00:36:57,466 --> 00:36:59,426
Well, there are people who are
expecting me too, you know.

579
00:36:59,593 --> 00:37:00,928
We both made promises.

580
00:37:01,095 --> 00:37:02,805
Not to each other.

581
00:37:03,222 --> 00:37:04,223
Wanda.

582
00:37:05,182 --> 00:37:07,518
For two years,
we've stolen these moments...

583
00:37:07,684 --> 00:37:09,728
trying to see
if this could work and...

584
00:37:09,895 --> 00:37:11,480
I don't know.

585
00:37:11,647 --> 00:37:13,607
You know what, I'm just
gonna speak for myself.

586
00:37:13,690 --> 00:37:15,484
I think...

587
00:37:15,651 --> 00:37:16,735
- It works.
- It works.

588
00:37:16,902 --> 00:37:18,195
It works.

589
00:37:20,656 --> 00:37:21,907
Stay.

590
00:37:22,825 --> 00:37:24,493
Stay with me.

591
00:37:29,248 --> 00:37:32,501
Or not. If I'm overstepping...

592
00:37:39,550 --> 00:37:41,301
What are they?

593
00:37:41,635 --> 00:37:44,054
What the stone
was warning me about.

594
00:37:54,022 --> 00:37:55,357
I have to go.

595
00:37:55,441 --> 00:37:56,442
No, Vision.

596
00:37:57,067 --> 00:37:58,318
Vision, if that's true,

597
00:37:58,402 --> 00:38:01,196
then maybe
going isn't the best idea.

598
00:38:02,239 --> 00:38:03,323
Wanda, I...

599
00:38:03,490 --> 00:38:05,534
Vision!

600
00:38:33,687 --> 00:38:36,356
The blade,
it stopped me from phasing.

601
00:38:37,274 --> 00:38:39,234
- Is that even possible?
- It isn't supposed to be.

602
00:38:40,319 --> 00:38:42,029
My systems are failing.

603
00:38:42,946 --> 00:38:45,616
I'm beginning to think
we should have stayed in bed.

604
00:38:48,160 --> 00:38:49,369
Vis!

605
00:38:58,253 --> 00:39:01,632
Give up the stone,
and she lives.

606
00:39:39,753 --> 00:39:40,963
Hands off.

607
00:39:56,770 --> 00:39:58,021
Come on. Come on.

608
00:39:58,188 --> 00:39:59,982
Come on, you gotta get up.

609
00:40:00,148 --> 00:40:02,359
You gotta get up.
Come on. Hey.

610
00:40:03,443 --> 00:40:04,861
Hey. We have to go.

611
00:40:06,780 --> 00:40:09,366
Please. Please leave.

612
00:40:09,491 --> 00:40:11,285
You asked me to stay.

613
00:40:12,536 --> 00:40:13,704
- I'm staying.
- Please.

614
00:41:24,900 --> 00:41:26,610
- Get up.
- I can't.

615
00:41:26,777 --> 00:41:29,488
We don't wanna kill you,
but we will.

616
00:41:29,655 --> 00:41:31,823
You'll never get
the chance again.

617
00:41:47,798 --> 00:41:49,341
Can you stand?

618
00:41:54,096 --> 00:41:55,514
Thank you, Captain.

619
00:41:58,225 --> 00:41:59,851
Let's get you on the jet.

620
00:42:03,814 --> 00:42:07,234
Now, I thought we had a deal.

621
00:42:07,401 --> 00:42:11,113
Stay close, check in,
don't take any chances.

622
00:42:11,279 --> 00:42:12,614
I'm sorry.

623
00:42:12,781 --> 00:42:14,574
We just wanted time.

624
00:42:17,285 --> 00:42:18,537
Where to, Cap?

625
00:42:21,373 --> 00:42:22,874
Home.

626
00:42:26,461 --> 00:42:28,505
We'll be safe.
We'll be safe.

627
00:42:53,071 --> 00:42:54,114
<i>Zehobereians.</i>

628
00:42:54,281 --> 00:42:56,032
Mother! Where's my mother?

629
00:42:56,199 --> 00:42:57,534
<i>Choose a side or die.</i>

630
00:42:57,701 --> 00:42:59,161
Mother!

631
00:42:59,327 --> 00:43:01,496
<i>One side
is a revelation...</i>

632
00:43:01,663 --> 00:43:04,708
<i>the other an honor
known only to a few.</i>

633
00:43:05,625 --> 00:43:07,085
What's wrong, little one?

634
00:43:07,711 --> 00:43:11,131
My mother. Where is my mother?

635
00:43:15,927 --> 00:43:17,137
What's your name?

636
00:43:18,472 --> 00:43:20,140
Gamora.

637
00:43:20,640 --> 00:43:22,768
You're quite the fighter,
Gamora.

638
00:43:24,311 --> 00:43:25,312
Come.

639
00:43:25,687 --> 00:43:26,688
Let me help you.

640
00:43:40,202 --> 00:43:41,328
Look.

641
00:43:44,998 --> 00:43:46,666
Pretty, isn't it?

642
00:43:47,417 --> 00:43:50,879
Perfectly balanced,
as all things should be.

643
00:43:51,046 --> 00:43:54,800
Too much to one side
or the other...

644
00:43:58,804 --> 00:44:01,640
Here. You try.

645
00:44:05,393 --> 00:44:08,480
<i>Now, go in peace
to meet your maker.</i>

646
00:44:09,981 --> 00:44:11,817
Uh-uh.

647
00:44:13,735 --> 00:44:15,278
Concentrate.

648
00:44:18,240 --> 00:44:21,034
There. You've got it.

649
00:44:30,544 --> 00:44:31,628
Gamora.

650
00:44:32,712 --> 00:44:33,797
Do you know if these grenades

651
00:44:33,880 --> 00:44:36,049
are the blow-off-your-junk
kind or the gas kind?

652
00:44:36,216 --> 00:44:37,300
Because I was thinking about

653
00:44:37,384 --> 00:44:38,969
hanging a couple
on my belt right here.

654
00:44:39,052 --> 00:44:40,136
But I don't want to
if they're the...

655
00:44:40,220 --> 00:44:41,471
I need to ask a favor.

656
00:44:42,389 --> 00:44:43,723
Yeah, sure.

657
00:44:45,267 --> 00:44:46,351
One way or another,

658
00:44:46,434 --> 00:44:48,687
the path that we're on
leads to Thanos.

659
00:44:50,438 --> 00:44:51,940
Which is what
the grenades are for.

660
00:44:52,858 --> 00:44:55,193
Uh, I'm sorry.
What's the favor?

661
00:44:57,529 --> 00:44:58,530
If things go wrong...

662
00:45:00,115 --> 00:45:02,284
If Thanos gets me...

663
00:45:06,830 --> 00:45:08,790
I want you to promise me...

664
00:45:09,833 --> 00:45:10,959
you'll kill me.

665
00:45:11,710 --> 00:45:12,711
What?

666
00:45:15,881 --> 00:45:18,258
I know something he doesn't.

667
00:45:20,802 --> 00:45:23,013
And if he finds it out,

668
00:45:23,096 --> 00:45:24,472
the entire universe
could be at risk.

669
00:45:25,140 --> 00:45:26,224
What do you know?

670
00:45:26,391 --> 00:45:28,435
If I tell you, you'd know too.

671
00:45:31,479 --> 00:45:33,315
If it's so important...

672
00:45:33,481 --> 00:45:34,482
shouldn't I?

673
00:45:34,608 --> 00:45:35,817
Only if you wanna die.

674
00:45:35,984 --> 00:45:37,569
Why does somebody always
have to die in this scenario?

675
00:45:38,987 --> 00:45:39,988
Just...

676
00:45:42,407 --> 00:45:45,410
Trust me.
And possibly kill me.

677
00:45:45,577 --> 00:45:47,913
I mean, I'd like to.

678
00:45:48,079 --> 00:45:49,915
I really would. But you...

679
00:45:50,081 --> 00:45:51,291
Swear to me.

680
00:45:54,794 --> 00:45:57,088
Swear to me on your mother.

681
00:46:04,095 --> 00:46:05,096
Okay.

682
00:46:11,186 --> 00:46:12,312
Okay.

683
00:46:28,536 --> 00:46:29,579
- Oh.
- Dude.

684
00:46:29,663 --> 00:46:31,206
How long have you been
standing there?

685
00:46:31,289 --> 00:46:32,290
An hour.

686
00:46:32,832 --> 00:46:34,084
An hour?

687
00:46:34,626 --> 00:46:35,919
Are you serious?

688
00:46:36,086 --> 00:46:38,254
I've mastered the ability

689
00:46:38,338 --> 00:46:41,007
of standing
so incredibly still...

690
00:46:42,217 --> 00:46:44,803
that I become
invisible to the eye.

691
00:46:45,428 --> 00:46:46,429
Watch.

692
00:46:50,350 --> 00:46:51,935
You're eating a zarg-nut.

693
00:46:52,394 --> 00:46:53,812
But my movement...

694
00:46:54,646 --> 00:46:56,272
was so slow...

695
00:46:57,107 --> 00:46:58,942
that it's imperceptible.

696
00:46:59,109 --> 00:47:00,110
Mmm, no.

697
00:47:00,193 --> 00:47:02,529
I'm sure I'm invisible.

698
00:47:02,696 --> 00:47:03,863
Hi, Drax.

699
00:47:06,574 --> 00:47:07,575
Damn it.

700
00:47:27,470 --> 00:47:29,222
This place looks deserted.

701
00:47:29,389 --> 00:47:32,142
I'm reading movement
in the third quadrant.

702
00:47:32,308 --> 00:47:34,227
Yep,
I'm picking that up too.

703
00:47:35,645 --> 00:47:37,105
Let's put down right here.

704
00:47:48,867 --> 00:47:50,410
I don't have it.

705
00:47:52,537 --> 00:47:54,247
Everyone
in the galaxy knows

706
00:47:54,330 --> 00:47:55,749
you'd sell your own brother...

707
00:47:55,915 --> 00:47:57,542
if you thought it would add
even the slightest trinket...

708
00:47:57,709 --> 00:47:59,627
to your pathetic collection.

709
00:48:07,427 --> 00:48:09,846
I know you have
the Reality Stone, Tivan.

710
00:48:10,805 --> 00:48:14,267
Giving it to me will spare you
a great deal of suffering.

711
00:48:17,520 --> 00:48:19,105
I told you.

712
00:48:19,898 --> 00:48:20,899
I sold it.

713
00:48:23,777 --> 00:48:25,779
Why would I lie?

714
00:48:25,945 --> 00:48:28,156
I imagine it's like
breathing for you.

715
00:48:28,990 --> 00:48:30,700
Like suicide.

716
00:48:30,867 --> 00:48:32,368
You do understand.

717
00:48:33,328 --> 00:48:36,331
Not even you would surrender
something so precious.

718
00:48:36,498 --> 00:48:37,874
I didn't know what it was.

719
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:40,835
Then you're more of a fool
than I took you for.

720
00:48:41,211 --> 00:48:42,212
It's him.

721
00:48:42,378 --> 00:48:43,838
Last chance,
charlatan.

722
00:48:45,381 --> 00:48:47,342
Where's the stone?

723
00:48:47,509 --> 00:48:48,510
Today...

724
00:48:48,927 --> 00:48:49,928
Drax. Drax.

725
00:48:50,095 --> 00:48:52,055
...he pays for the deaths
of my wife and daughter.

726
00:48:52,138 --> 00:48:53,181
Drax, wait.

727
00:48:54,682 --> 00:48:56,059
Not yet, not yet, not yet.

728
00:48:56,226 --> 00:48:57,477
Drax.

729
00:49:01,356 --> 00:49:03,608
Drax, Drax, Drax.
Listen to me.

730
00:49:03,775 --> 00:49:06,027
He doesn't have the stone yet.

731
00:49:06,194 --> 00:49:07,821
If we get it,
then we can stop him.

732
00:49:08,655 --> 00:49:11,825
We have to get
the stone first. Yeah.

733
00:49:11,991 --> 00:49:13,076
No.

734
00:49:13,243 --> 00:49:16,287
No. For Ovette, for Camaria.

735
00:49:16,746 --> 00:49:18,039
Sleep.

736
00:49:29,968 --> 00:49:30,969
Okay.

737
00:49:31,136 --> 00:49:35,223
Gamora, Mantis, you go right.

738
00:49:36,599 --> 00:49:37,851
The other right.

739
00:50:02,167 --> 00:50:03,877
Why?

740
00:50:13,887 --> 00:50:17,974
Why you, daughter?

741
00:50:36,576 --> 00:50:37,577
That was quick.

742
00:50:43,374 --> 00:50:48,254
Magnificent! Magnificent!
Magnificent!

743
00:50:50,590 --> 00:50:53,301
<i>Is that sadness
I sense in you, daughter?</i>

744
00:50:56,429 --> 00:50:58,932
<i>In my heart,
I knew you still cared.</i>

745
00:51:06,314 --> 00:51:09,567
<i>But one never knows for sure.</i>

746
00:51:18,785 --> 00:51:21,621
<i>Reality is often
disappointing.</i>

747
00:51:24,791 --> 00:51:27,043
That is, it was.

748
00:51:29,087 --> 00:51:30,463
Now...

749
00:51:32,465 --> 00:51:35,260
reality can be
whatever I want.

750
00:51:36,803 --> 00:51:38,263
You knew I'd come.

751
00:51:38,429 --> 00:51:40,056
I counted on it.

752
00:51:40,848 --> 00:51:43,768
There's something we need
to discuss, little one.

753
00:51:48,398 --> 00:51:50,108
Thanos!

754
00:51:57,699 --> 00:51:58,741
No!

755
00:52:03,121 --> 00:52:04,706
Let her go, Grimace.

756
00:52:05,164 --> 00:52:06,165
Peter.

757
00:52:07,625 --> 00:52:08,876
I told you to go right.

758
00:52:09,460 --> 00:52:10,837
Now? Really?

759
00:52:11,004 --> 00:52:12,422
You let her go!

760
00:52:12,839 --> 00:52:14,549
Ah, the boyfriend.

761
00:52:14,716 --> 00:52:15,717
No.

762
00:52:15,883 --> 00:52:17,051
Like to think of myself

763
00:52:17,135 --> 00:52:19,595
more as a Titan-killing,
long-term booty call.

764
00:52:19,762 --> 00:52:21,806
- Let her go.
- Peter.

765
00:52:21,973 --> 00:52:26,686
I'm gonna blow that nutsack
of a chin right off your face.

766
00:52:27,270 --> 00:52:28,771
Not him.

767
00:52:39,240 --> 00:52:42,952
You promised. You promised.

768
00:52:47,123 --> 00:52:48,333
Oh, daughter.

769
00:52:48,791 --> 00:52:51,294
You expect too much from him.

770
00:52:54,881 --> 00:52:56,466
She's asked, hasn't she?

771
00:53:00,428 --> 00:53:01,429
Do it.

772
00:53:05,266 --> 00:53:06,517
Mmm.

773
00:53:07,769 --> 00:53:09,187
Do it!

774
00:53:15,943 --> 00:53:17,362
I told you to go right.

775
00:53:19,322 --> 00:53:22,283
I love you more than anything.

776
00:53:25,411 --> 00:53:26,913
I love you too.

777
00:53:41,219 --> 00:53:42,261
I like him.

778
00:54:13,084 --> 00:54:14,919
<i>Still no word from Vision?</i>

779
00:54:15,044 --> 00:54:17,672
Satellites lost him
somewhere over Edinburgh.

780
00:54:18,297 --> 00:54:19,340
<i>On a stolen Quin jet</i>

781
00:54:19,424 --> 00:54:21,217
<i>with four of the world's
most wanted criminals.</i>

782
00:54:21,676 --> 00:54:23,261
You know they're
only criminals because

783
00:54:23,344 --> 00:54:24,846
you've chosen to
call them that, right, sir?

784
00:54:25,012 --> 00:54:26,139
<i>My God, Rhodes.</i>

785
00:54:26,305 --> 00:54:29,517
<i>Your talent for horseshit
rivals my own.</i>

786
00:54:29,684 --> 00:54:30,810
If it weren't
for those Accords,

787
00:54:30,893 --> 00:54:32,270
Vision would've been
right here.

788
00:54:33,020 --> 00:54:36,232
<i>I remember your signature
on those papers, Colonel.</i>

789
00:54:36,732 --> 00:54:37,733
That's right.

790
00:54:39,735 --> 00:54:41,571
And I'm pretty sure
I paid for that.

791
00:54:41,737 --> 00:54:42,947
<i>You have second thoughts?</i>

792
00:54:43,114 --> 00:54:44,824
Not anymore.

793
00:54:50,663 --> 00:54:52,248
Mr. Secretary.

794
00:54:56,794 --> 00:54:58,463
<i>You got some nerve.</i>

795
00:54:59,130 --> 00:55:00,756
<i>I'll give you that.</i>

796
00:55:00,923 --> 00:55:02,675
You could use
some of that right now.

797
00:55:03,509 --> 00:55:05,761
<i>The world's on fire.</i>

798
00:55:06,554 --> 00:55:09,640
<i>And you think all is forgiven?</i>

799
00:55:10,224 --> 00:55:12,101
I'm not looking
for forgiveness.

800
00:55:12,185 --> 00:55:14,312
And I'm way past
asking permission.

801
00:55:16,272 --> 00:55:18,316
Earth just lost
her best defender.

802
00:55:18,816 --> 00:55:20,026
So we're here to fight.

803
00:55:21,611 --> 00:55:23,529
And if you wanna
stand in our way...

804
00:55:24,530 --> 00:55:26,449
we'll fight you too.

805
00:55:29,702 --> 00:55:30,703
<i>Arrest them.</i>

806
00:55:31,829 --> 00:55:33,414
All over it.

807
00:55:38,503 --> 00:55:39,879
That's a court-martial.

808
00:55:42,340 --> 00:55:43,341
It's great to see you, Cap.

809
00:55:44,467 --> 00:55:46,219
You too, Rhodey.

810
00:55:46,302 --> 00:55:47,303
Hey.

811
00:55:48,638 --> 00:55:50,932
Wow. You guys...

812
00:55:51,766 --> 00:55:53,768
really look like crap.

813
00:55:53,935 --> 00:55:55,520
Must've been
a rough couple years.

814
00:55:55,686 --> 00:55:58,356
Yeah, well, the hotels
weren't exactly five star.

815
00:55:58,814 --> 00:56:00,983
Uh, I think
you look great.

816
00:56:04,320 --> 00:56:05,404
Uh...

817
00:56:08,074 --> 00:56:10,117
Yeah, I'm back.

818
00:56:11,786 --> 00:56:12,787
Hi, Bruce.

819
00:56:18,334 --> 00:56:19,335
Nat.

820
00:56:22,755 --> 00:56:24,298
This is awkward.

821
00:56:26,801 --> 00:56:28,344
So we gotta assume
they're coming back, right?

822
00:56:28,511 --> 00:56:29,679
And they can clearly find us.

823
00:56:29,845 --> 00:56:32,056
We need all hands on deck.
Where's Clint?

824
00:56:32,348 --> 00:56:33,808
After the whole
Accords situation,

825
00:56:33,933 --> 00:56:35,434
he and Scott took a deal.
It was too tough

826
00:56:35,601 --> 00:56:37,144
on their families.
They're on house arrest.

827
00:56:37,270 --> 00:56:38,563
- Who's Scott?
- Ant-Man.

828
00:56:38,729 --> 00:56:40,189
There's an Ant-Man
and a Spider-Man?

829
00:56:41,107 --> 00:56:42,149
Okay, look.

830
00:56:42,233 --> 00:56:45,069
Thanos has the biggest army
in the universe...

831
00:56:45,236 --> 00:56:48,656
and he is not gonna stop
until he gets...

832
00:56:50,491 --> 00:56:51,534
Vision's stone.

833
00:56:51,701 --> 00:56:52,952
Then we have to protect it.

834
00:56:53,119 --> 00:56:54,745
No, we have to destroy it.

835
00:56:56,914 --> 00:56:58,207
I've been giving
a good deal of thought

836
00:56:58,291 --> 00:56:59,292
to this entity in my head.

837
00:56:59,458 --> 00:57:00,960
About its nature.

838
00:57:01,502 --> 00:57:03,671
But also its composition.

839
00:57:03,838 --> 00:57:05,840
I think if it were exposed

840
00:57:05,923 --> 00:57:07,758
to a sufficiently powerful
energy source...

841
00:57:07,925 --> 00:57:11,762
something very similar to
its own signature, perhaps...

842
00:57:13,347 --> 00:57:15,516
its molecular integrity
could fail.

843
00:57:16,058 --> 00:57:18,311
Yeah, and you with it.

844
00:57:18,769 --> 00:57:20,229
We're not having
this conversation.

845
00:57:20,396 --> 00:57:22,398
Eliminating the stone
is the only way

846
00:57:22,481 --> 00:57:24,483
to be certain that
Thanos can't get it.

847
00:57:25,026 --> 00:57:27,236
That's too high a price.

848
00:57:31,741 --> 00:57:34,118
Only you have
the power to pay it.

849
00:57:38,372 --> 00:57:40,416
Thanos threatens
half the universe.

850
00:57:40,583 --> 00:57:43,127
One life cannot stand
in the way of defeating him.

851
00:57:43,294 --> 00:57:44,712
But it should.

852
00:57:47,214 --> 00:57:48,591
We don't trade lives, Vision.

853
00:57:48,758 --> 00:57:50,718
Captain, 70 years ago,
you laid down your life...

854
00:57:50,885 --> 00:57:52,678
to save how many
millions of people?

855
00:57:52,845 --> 00:57:54,889
Tell me,
why is this any different?

856
00:57:55,056 --> 00:57:57,350
Because you might
have a choice.

857
00:57:58,643 --> 00:57:59,977
Your mind is made up

858
00:58:00,061 --> 00:58:02,438
of a complex construct
of overlays.

859
00:58:02,605 --> 00:58:06,192
Jarvis, Ultron,
Tony, me, the stone.

860
00:58:06,359 --> 00:58:08,110
All of them mixed together,

861
00:58:08,194 --> 00:58:09,695
all of them
learning from one another.

862
00:58:10,071 --> 00:58:11,822
You're saying Vision isn't
just the stone?

863
00:58:11,989 --> 00:58:15,076
I'm saying that
if we take out the stone...

864
00:58:15,242 --> 00:58:16,661
there's still a whole lot
of Vision left.

865
00:58:16,744 --> 00:58:18,204
Perhaps the best parts.

866
00:58:18,537 --> 00:58:19,872
Can we do that?

867
00:58:20,581 --> 00:58:21,624
Not me, not here.

868
00:58:22,625 --> 00:58:24,168
Well,
you better find someone

869
00:58:24,251 --> 00:58:25,419
and somewhere fast.

870
00:58:25,586 --> 00:58:26,962
Ross isn't just gonna
let you guys

871
00:58:27,046 --> 00:58:28,255
have your old rooms back.

872
00:58:31,300 --> 00:58:32,885
I know somewhere.

873
00:58:47,525 --> 00:58:48,776
The Kingsguard

874
00:58:48,859 --> 00:58:50,152
and the Dora Milaje
have been alerted.

875
00:58:50,319 --> 00:58:51,862
And the Border Tribe?

876
00:58:52,321 --> 00:58:53,906
Those that are left.

877
00:58:54,198 --> 00:58:56,325
Send word
to the Jabari as well.

878
00:58:56,492 --> 00:58:58,577
M'Baku likes a good fight.

879
00:59:00,871 --> 00:59:02,581
And what of this one?

880
00:59:03,207 --> 00:59:05,334
This one may be tired of war.

881
00:59:05,668 --> 00:59:08,713
But the White Wolf
has rested long enough.

882
00:59:31,360 --> 00:59:32,945
Where's the fight?

883
00:59:33,863 --> 00:59:35,281
On its way.

884
00:59:53,674 --> 00:59:56,260
In all the time
I've served Thanos...

885
00:59:58,137 --> 01:00:00,139
I have never failed him.

886
01:00:05,227 --> 01:00:08,314
If I were to reach
our rendezvous on Titan...

887
01:00:08,481 --> 01:00:10,065
with the Time Stone
still attached

888
01:00:10,149 --> 01:00:12,318
to your vaguely
irritating person...

889
01:00:12,485 --> 01:00:15,070
there would be judgment.

890
01:00:23,662 --> 01:00:25,206
Give me...

891
01:00:29,043 --> 01:00:30,044
The stone.

892
01:00:42,640 --> 01:00:43,891
Wow, you're a seriously

893
01:00:43,974 --> 01:00:45,059
loyal piece of outerwear,
aren't you?

894
01:00:45,226 --> 01:00:47,228
Yeah, uh,
speaking of loyalty...

895
01:00:47,812 --> 01:00:48,813
What the...

896
01:00:48,979 --> 01:00:50,731
- I know what you're gonna say.
- You should not be here.

897
01:00:50,898 --> 01:00:51,941
- I was gonna go home.
- I don't wanna hear it.

898
01:00:52,107 --> 01:00:53,108
But it was such a long way
down and I just thought

899
01:00:53,192 --> 01:00:54,443
- about you on the way...
- And now I gotta hear it.

900
01:00:54,527 --> 01:00:55,528
...and kinda stuck to the side
of the ship.

901
01:00:55,694 --> 01:00:57,738
And this suit is ridiculously
intuitive, by the way.

902
01:00:57,905 --> 01:00:58,906
God damn it.

903
01:00:59,073 --> 01:01:01,867
So, if anything, it's kinda
your fault that I'm here.

904
01:01:02,034 --> 01:01:03,369
- What did you just say?
- I take that back.

905
01:01:03,536 --> 01:01:04,829
And now, I'm here in space.

906
01:01:04,995 --> 01:01:07,414
Yeah, right where
I didn't want you to be.

907
01:01:07,581 --> 01:01:09,667
This isn't Coney Island.
This isn't a field trip.

908
01:01:09,834 --> 01:01:11,085
This is a one-way ticket.

909
01:01:11,168 --> 01:01:12,711
You hear me? Don't pretend
you thought this through.

910
01:01:12,795 --> 01:01:13,796
No, I did think this through.

911
01:01:13,879 --> 01:01:15,506
You could not have possibly
thought this through.

912
01:01:15,673 --> 01:01:17,174
You can't be a friendly
neighborhood Spider-Man...

913
01:01:17,341 --> 01:01:18,926
if there's no neighborhood.

914
01:01:21,095 --> 01:01:22,221
Okay, that didn't
really make sense,

915
01:01:22,304 --> 01:01:23,639
but you know
what I'm trying to say.

916
01:01:25,766 --> 01:01:28,644
Come on. We got a situation.

917
01:01:29,645 --> 01:01:30,646
See him down there?
He's in trouble.

918
01:01:30,729 --> 01:01:31,730
What's your plan?

919
01:01:31,814 --> 01:01:32,982
- Go.
- Um...

920
01:01:33,649 --> 01:01:35,067
Okay, okay... Uh...

921
01:01:35,359 --> 01:01:38,571
Okay. Did you ever see
this really old movie, <i>Aliens?</i>

922
01:01:42,283 --> 01:01:44,368
Painful, aren't they?

923
01:01:45,160 --> 01:01:48,122
They were originally designed
for microsurgery.

924
01:01:48,789 --> 01:01:50,875
And any one of them...

925
01:01:55,963 --> 01:01:58,173
Could end your friend's life
in an instant.

926
01:01:58,757 --> 01:02:00,384
<i>I gotta tell you,
he's not really my friend.</i>

927
01:02:00,551 --> 01:02:03,220
<i>Saving his life is more
of a professional courtesy.</i>

928
01:02:05,014 --> 01:02:06,765
You've saved nothing.

929
01:02:07,641 --> 01:02:09,643
Your powers
are inconsequential

930
01:02:09,727 --> 01:02:10,936
compared to mine.

931
01:02:11,353 --> 01:02:12,980
Yeah, but the kid's
seen more movies.

932
01:02:27,161 --> 01:02:29,330
Yes! Wait.
What are those?

933
01:02:44,970 --> 01:02:46,680
Hey,
we haven't officially met.

934
01:02:47,973 --> 01:02:49,058
Cool.

935
01:02:51,060 --> 01:02:52,519
We gotta turn
this ship around.

936
01:02:52,645 --> 01:02:54,688
Yeah, now he wants
to run. Great plan.

937
01:02:54,855 --> 01:02:56,231
No, I want to protect
the stone.

938
01:02:56,398 --> 01:02:57,608
And I want you
to thank me.

939
01:02:57,691 --> 01:02:59,193
Now, go ahead. I'm listening.

940
01:02:59,360 --> 01:03:02,071
For what?
Nearly blasting me into space?

941
01:03:02,237 --> 01:03:04,490
Who just saved
your magical ass? Me.

942
01:03:04,657 --> 01:03:05,658
I seriously don't know

943
01:03:05,741 --> 01:03:06,909
how you fit your head
into that helmet.

944
01:03:07,076 --> 01:03:09,328
Admit it, you should've
ducked out when I told you to.

945
01:03:09,495 --> 01:03:10,996
I tried to bench you.
You refused.

946
01:03:11,163 --> 01:03:13,082
Unlike everyone else in your
life, I don't work for you.

947
01:03:13,248 --> 01:03:14,833
And due to that fact,

948
01:03:14,917 --> 01:03:16,251
we're now
in a flying doughnut...

949
01:03:16,418 --> 01:03:18,087
billions of miles from Earth
with no backup.

950
01:03:18,253 --> 01:03:20,172
- I'm backup.
- No, you're a stowaway.

951
01:03:20,339 --> 01:03:21,340
The adults are talking.

952
01:03:21,507 --> 01:03:24,093
I'm sorry, I'm confused
as to the relationship here.

953
01:03:24,259 --> 01:03:25,886
What is he, your ward?

954
01:03:26,053 --> 01:03:27,054
No.

955
01:03:27,554 --> 01:03:29,431
- I'm Peter, by the way.
- Doctor Strange.

956
01:03:29,598 --> 01:03:31,308
Oh, you're using
our made-up names. Um...

957
01:03:32,267 --> 01:03:33,477
I'm Spider-Man, then.

958
01:03:34,436 --> 01:03:35,938
This ship is
self-correcting its course.

959
01:03:36,021 --> 01:03:37,022
Thing's on autopilot.

960
01:03:37,189 --> 01:03:38,899
Can we control it?

961
01:03:39,066 --> 01:03:40,985
Fly us home?

962
01:03:43,988 --> 01:03:44,989
- Stark?
- Yeah.

963
01:03:45,155 --> 01:03:46,407
Can you get us home?

964
01:03:46,573 --> 01:03:47,825
Yeah, I heard you.

965
01:03:49,118 --> 01:03:51,578
I'm thinking I'm not
so sure we should.

966
01:03:52,246 --> 01:03:53,747
Under no circumstances

967
01:03:53,831 --> 01:03:56,375
can we bring
the Time Stone to Thanos.

968
01:03:56,542 --> 01:03:57,710
I don't think
you quite understand

969
01:03:57,793 --> 01:03:58,794
what's at stake here.

970
01:03:58,961 --> 01:04:01,296
What? No. It's you
who doesn't understand...

971
01:04:01,463 --> 01:04:04,216
that Thanos has been
inside my head for six years.

972
01:04:04,383 --> 01:04:05,968
Since he sent an army
to New York

973
01:04:06,051 --> 01:04:07,594
and now he's back.

974
01:04:07,761 --> 01:04:09,680
And I don't know what to do.

975
01:04:09,847 --> 01:04:11,015
So I'm not so sure

976
01:04:11,098 --> 01:04:12,891
if it's a better plan to fight
him on our turf or his...

977
01:04:13,058 --> 01:04:16,687
but you saw what they did,
what they can do.

978
01:04:16,854 --> 01:04:19,064
At least on his turf,
he's not expecting it.

979
01:04:19,231 --> 01:04:21,984
So I say we take
the fight to him.

980
01:04:22,151 --> 01:04:23,152
Doctor.

981
01:04:24,862 --> 01:04:26,530
Do you concur?

982
01:04:28,991 --> 01:04:31,577
All right, Stark.
We go to him.

983
01:04:32,661 --> 01:04:34,705
But you have to understand...

984
01:04:34,872 --> 01:04:36,540
if it comes to saving you

985
01:04:36,623 --> 01:04:39,084
or the kid
or the Time Stone...

986
01:04:39,251 --> 01:04:42,087
I will not hesitate
to let either of you die.

987
01:04:42,921 --> 01:04:46,592
I can't, because the universe
depends on it.

988
01:04:47,176 --> 01:04:50,054
Nice. Good, moral compass.

989
01:04:51,346 --> 01:04:52,848
We're straight.

990
01:04:53,974 --> 01:04:55,476
All right, kid.

991
01:04:56,769 --> 01:04:57,811
You're an Avenger now.

992
01:05:34,389 --> 01:05:36,683
I thought
you might be hungry.

993
01:05:48,821 --> 01:05:50,364
I always hated that chair.

994
01:05:50,572 --> 01:05:52,616
So I've been told.

995
01:05:53,283 --> 01:05:57,204
Even so, I'd hoped you'd
sit in it one day.

996
01:05:57,955 --> 01:05:59,456
I hated this room.

997
01:06:00,374 --> 01:06:01,667
This ship.

998
01:06:01,834 --> 01:06:03,627
I hated my life.

999
01:06:08,048 --> 01:06:10,300
You told me that too.

1000
01:06:13,470 --> 01:06:14,847
Every day.

1001
01:06:17,641 --> 01:06:19,601
For almost 20 years.

1002
01:06:22,146 --> 01:06:24,565
I was a child
when you took me.

1003
01:06:25,440 --> 01:06:26,733
I saved you.

1004
01:06:30,279 --> 01:06:31,280
No.

1005
01:06:32,781 --> 01:06:36,285
No. We were happy
on my home planet.

1006
01:06:36,493 --> 01:06:37,619
Going to bed hungry...

1007
01:06:38,162 --> 01:06:39,830
scrounging for scraps.

1008
01:06:40,038 --> 01:06:42,916
Your planet was
on the brink of collapse.

1009
01:06:43,000 --> 01:06:45,043
I'm the one who stopped that.

1010
01:06:45,544 --> 01:06:47,379
Do you know
what's happened since then?

1011
01:06:47,546 --> 01:06:49,173
The children born...

1012
01:06:49,798 --> 01:06:53,177
have known nothing but
full bellies and clear skies.

1013
01:06:53,343 --> 01:06:54,595
It's a paradise.

1014
01:06:57,264 --> 01:06:59,141
Because you murdered
half the planet.

1015
01:06:59,266 --> 01:07:02,144
A small price to pay
for salvation.

1016
01:07:02,352 --> 01:07:03,353
You're insane.

1017
01:07:03,520 --> 01:07:05,480
Little one,
it's a simple calculus.

1018
01:07:05,606 --> 01:07:08,400
This universe is finite,
its resources finite.

1019
01:07:08,984 --> 01:07:12,946
If life is left unchecked,
life will cease to exist.

1020
01:07:13,405 --> 01:07:14,489
It needs correction.

1021
01:07:14,615 --> 01:07:15,991
You don't know that!

1022
01:07:17,576 --> 01:07:19,578
I'm the only one
who knows that.

1023
01:07:20,412 --> 01:07:24,583
At least, I'm the only one
with the will to act on it.

1024
01:07:26,210 --> 01:07:27,753
For a time...

1025
01:07:29,796 --> 01:07:34,051
you had that same will...

1026
01:07:35,636 --> 01:07:38,055
as you fought by my side.

1027
01:07:38,931 --> 01:07:39,973
Daughter.

1028
01:07:40,766 --> 01:07:42,559
I'm not your daughter.

1029
01:07:44,937 --> 01:07:47,689
Everything I hate about myself
you taught me.

1030
01:07:48,523 --> 01:07:49,942
And, in doing so,

1031
01:07:50,025 --> 01:07:52,236
made you the fiercest woman
in the galaxy.

1032
01:07:55,197 --> 01:07:57,991
That's why I trusted you
to find the Soul Stone.

1033
01:08:01,411 --> 01:08:03,872
I'm sorry I disappointed you.

1034
01:08:05,374 --> 01:08:07,167
I am disappointed.

1035
01:08:07,960 --> 01:08:10,420
But not because
you didn't find it.

1036
01:08:14,132 --> 01:08:15,759
But because you did.

1037
01:08:17,219 --> 01:08:18,971
And you lied.

1038
01:08:36,071 --> 01:08:37,197
Nebula.

1039
01:08:44,454 --> 01:08:45,789
Don't do this.

1040
01:08:45,956 --> 01:08:47,165
Some time ago,

1041
01:08:47,249 --> 01:08:49,960
your sister snuck aboard
this ship to kill me.

1042
01:08:50,127 --> 01:08:51,128
Please don't do this.

1043
01:08:51,211 --> 01:08:53,505
And very nearly succeeded.

1044
01:08:54,172 --> 01:08:55,632
So I brought her here.

1045
01:08:57,175 --> 01:08:58,427
To talk.

1046
01:09:06,059 --> 01:09:08,478
Stop. Stop it.

1047
01:09:14,359 --> 01:09:16,695
I swear to you on my life.

1048
01:09:17,195 --> 01:09:19,489
I never found the Soul Stone.

1049
01:09:23,618 --> 01:09:25,203
<i>Accessing memory files.</i>

1050
01:09:25,370 --> 01:09:26,705
<i>You know
what he's about to do.</i>

1051
01:09:26,872 --> 01:09:29,458
<i>He's finally ready,
and he's going for the stones.</i>

1052
01:09:29,624 --> 01:09:30,751
<i>-All of them.
- He can never get them all.</i>

1053
01:09:30,876 --> 01:09:31,877
<i>He will!</i>

1054
01:09:31,960 --> 01:09:33,920
<i>He can't, Nebula.</i>

1055
01:09:34,087 --> 01:09:36,423
<i>Because I found the map
to the Soul Stone...</i>

1056
01:09:36,590 --> 01:09:39,384
<i>and I burned it to ash.
I burned it.</i>

1057
01:09:44,431 --> 01:09:46,224
You're strong.

1058
01:09:48,268 --> 01:09:49,269
Me.

1059
01:09:51,855 --> 01:09:53,440
You're generous.

1060
01:09:54,775 --> 01:09:55,776
Me.

1061
01:09:57,778 --> 01:10:00,197
But I never taught you to lie.

1062
01:10:00,364 --> 01:10:02,991
That's why
you're so bad at it.

1063
01:10:05,202 --> 01:10:09,748
Where is the Soul Stone?

1064
01:10:27,140 --> 01:10:28,725
Vormir!

1065
01:10:46,284 --> 01:10:47,869
The stone is on Vormir.

1066
01:10:51,206 --> 01:10:53,375
Show me.

1067
01:10:55,460 --> 01:10:56,795
I am Groot.

1068
01:10:56,962 --> 01:10:58,088
Tinkle in the cup.

1069
01:10:58,171 --> 01:10:59,506
We're not looking.
What's there to see?

1070
01:10:59,673 --> 01:11:01,842
What's a twig? Everybody's
seen a twig before.

1071
01:11:02,008 --> 01:11:03,093
I am Groot.

1072
01:11:03,260 --> 01:11:04,302
Tree, pour what's in the cup

1073
01:11:04,386 --> 01:11:05,887
out into space
and go in the cup again.

1074
01:11:06,179 --> 01:11:07,389
You speak Groot?

1075
01:11:07,556 --> 01:11:09,349
Yes, they taught it on Asgard.
It was an elective.

1076
01:11:09,516 --> 01:11:10,559
I am Groot.

1077
01:11:10,725 --> 01:11:12,727
You'll know when we're close.

1078
01:11:12,894 --> 01:11:14,479
Nidavellir's forge harnesses

1079
01:11:14,563 --> 01:11:16,773
the blazing power
of a neutron star.

1080
01:11:19,609 --> 01:11:21,611
It's the birthplace
of my hammer.

1081
01:11:22,320 --> 01:11:24,072
It's truly awesome.

1082
01:11:30,120 --> 01:11:33,248
Okay, time to be the captain.

1083
01:11:38,253 --> 01:11:39,796
So, dead brother, huh?

1084
01:11:40,464 --> 01:11:42,299
Yeah, that could be annoying.

1085
01:11:42,799 --> 01:11:44,676
Well, he's been dead before.

1086
01:11:46,136 --> 01:11:48,680
But, no, this time I think
it really might be true.

1087
01:11:49,139 --> 01:11:51,475
And you said
your sister and your dad?

1088
01:11:51,641 --> 01:11:52,934
Both dead.

1089
01:11:53,560 --> 01:11:55,228
But still got a mom, though?

1090
01:11:55,729 --> 01:11:56,980
Killed by a dark elf.

1091
01:11:57,147 --> 01:11:58,148
A best friend?

1092
01:11:58,273 --> 01:11:59,608
Stabbed through the heart.

1093
01:12:02,986 --> 01:12:06,156
You sure you're up to this
particular murder mission?

1094
01:12:08,408 --> 01:12:09,868
Absolutely.

1095
01:12:10,035 --> 01:12:13,538
Rage and vengeance,
anger, loss, regret...

1096
01:12:13,705 --> 01:12:15,290
they're all
tremendous motivators.

1097
01:12:15,373 --> 01:12:16,374
They really clear the mind.

1098
01:12:16,541 --> 01:12:18,168
So I'm good to go.

1099
01:12:18,835 --> 01:12:21,004
Yeah, but this Thanos
we're talkin' about...

1100
01:12:21,463 --> 01:12:23,757
he's the toughest there is.

1101
01:12:23,924 --> 01:12:25,967
- Well, he's never fought me.
- Yeah, he has.

1102
01:12:26,134 --> 01:12:27,677
He's never fought me twice.

1103
01:12:28,303 --> 01:12:30,055
And I'm getting a new hammer,
don't forget.

1104
01:12:30,222 --> 01:12:32,474
It better be some hammer.

1105
01:12:36,603 --> 01:12:38,980
You know, I'm 1,500 years old.

1106
01:12:39,648 --> 01:12:41,691
I've killed twice
as many enemies as that.

1107
01:12:41,858 --> 01:12:43,818
And every one of them
would've rather killed me,

1108
01:12:43,902 --> 01:12:44,903
but none succeeded.

1109
01:12:45,570 --> 01:12:48,490
I'm only alive
because fate wants me alive.

1110
01:12:48,657 --> 01:12:51,451
Thanos is just the latest
in a long line of bastards...

1111
01:12:51,618 --> 01:12:53,495
and he'll be the latest
to feel my vengeance.

1112
01:12:53,662 --> 01:12:55,455
Fate wills it so.

1113
01:12:55,539 --> 01:12:56,873
Mmm-hmm.

1114
01:12:56,957 --> 01:12:58,792
And what if you're wrong?

1115
01:13:02,087 --> 01:13:03,880
If I'm wrong, then...

1116
01:13:05,173 --> 01:13:06,716
what more could I lose?

1117
01:13:20,522 --> 01:13:21,898
I could lose a lot.

1118
01:13:21,982 --> 01:13:24,109
Me, personally,
I could lose a lot.

1119
01:13:27,904 --> 01:13:28,905
Okay.

1120
01:13:31,992 --> 01:13:34,077
If fate does want you
to kill that crap sack...

1121
01:13:34,244 --> 01:13:35,954
you're gonna need more
than one stupid eyeball.

1122
01:13:36,121 --> 01:13:38,123
- What's this?
- What's it look like?

1123
01:13:38,456 --> 01:13:40,875
Some jerk lost a bet with me
on Contraxia.

1124
01:13:41,209 --> 01:13:42,294
He gave you his eye?

1125
01:13:42,460 --> 01:13:43,587
No, he gave me 100 credits.

1126
01:13:43,753 --> 01:13:46,715
I snuck into his room later
that night and stole his eye.

1127
01:13:48,633 --> 01:13:49,884
Thank you, sweet rabbit.

1128
01:13:49,968 --> 01:13:51,011
Hmm..

1129
01:13:53,513 --> 01:13:55,015
Huh?

1130
01:13:56,808 --> 01:13:57,851
Oh.

1131
01:13:58,184 --> 01:14:00,854
I would've washed that.

1132
01:14:00,937 --> 01:14:03,398
The only way I could sneak it
off Contraxia was up my...

1133
01:14:04,774 --> 01:14:05,859
Hey, we're here!

1134
01:14:09,863 --> 01:14:10,989
I don't think
this thing works.

1135
01:14:11,156 --> 01:14:12,324
Everything seems dark.

1136
01:14:14,784 --> 01:14:16,494
It ain't the eye.

1137
01:14:29,841 --> 01:14:31,217
Something's wrong.

1138
01:14:32,010 --> 01:14:33,553
The star's gone out.

1139
01:14:34,679 --> 01:14:35,972
And the rings are frozen.

1140
01:14:57,118 --> 01:14:58,578
I hope
these dwarves are better

1141
01:14:58,662 --> 01:15:00,413
at forging
than they are cleaning.

1142
01:15:05,669 --> 01:15:07,253
Maybe they realized
that they live

1143
01:15:07,337 --> 01:15:08,755
in a junk pile
in the middle of space.

1144
01:15:08,922 --> 01:15:11,883
This forge hasn't gone dark
in centuries.

1145
01:15:14,177 --> 01:15:16,805
You said Thanos
had a gauntlet, right?

1146
01:15:16,971 --> 01:15:18,139
Yes, why?

1147
01:15:18,306 --> 01:15:20,350
It look
anything like that?

1148
01:15:23,770 --> 01:15:25,522
I am Groot.

1149
01:15:25,689 --> 01:15:27,190
Go back to the pod.

1150
01:15:31,194 --> 01:15:32,237
Eitri, wait!

1151
01:15:33,238 --> 01:15:34,239
Stop!

1152
01:15:35,156 --> 01:15:36,157
Stop.

1153
01:15:36,866 --> 01:15:37,867
Thor?

1154
01:15:41,204 --> 01:15:42,580
What happened here?

1155
01:15:42,997 --> 01:15:45,291
You were supposed
to protect us.

1156
01:15:46,209 --> 01:15:48,837
Asgard was supposed
to protect us.

1157
01:15:49,003 --> 01:15:51,214
Asgard is destroyed.

1158
01:15:53,466 --> 01:15:57,303
Eitri, the glove.
What did you do?

1159
01:16:10,066 --> 01:16:13,069
300 dwarves
lived on this ring.

1160
01:16:14,446 --> 01:16:17,365
I thought if I did what
he asked, they'd be safe.

1161
01:16:19,868 --> 01:16:21,327
I made what he wanted.

1162
01:16:23,037 --> 01:16:27,375
A device capable of harnessing
the power of the stones.

1163
01:16:31,921 --> 01:16:34,507
Then he killed
everyone anyway.

1164
01:16:36,593 --> 01:16:38,386
All except me.

1165
01:16:39,471 --> 01:16:41,347
"Your life is yours," he said.

1166
01:16:42,640 --> 01:16:46,603
"But your hands
are mine alone."

1167
01:16:47,562 --> 01:16:49,564
Eitri, this isn't about
your hands.

1168
01:16:50,690 --> 01:16:52,275
Every weapon
you've ever designed,

1169
01:16:52,358 --> 01:16:53,777
every axe, hammer, sword...

1170
01:16:53,943 --> 01:16:56,154
it's all inside your head.

1171
01:16:57,030 --> 01:16:58,948
Now, I know it feels
like all hope is lost.

1172
01:16:59,115 --> 01:17:00,658
Trust me, I know.

1173
01:17:01,117 --> 01:17:05,830
But together, you and I,
we can kill Thanos.

1174
01:17:46,329 --> 01:17:48,623
Mantis, listen very carefully.

1175
01:17:48,790 --> 01:17:51,000
I need you
to meet me on Titan.

1176
01:17:57,549 --> 01:17:58,675
Hey, what's going on?

1177
01:17:58,842 --> 01:18:00,051
I think we're here.

1178
01:18:00,218 --> 01:18:02,679
I don't think this rig has
a self-park function.

1179
01:18:04,430 --> 01:18:05,974
Get your hand
inside the steering gimbal.

1180
01:18:06,057 --> 01:18:07,100
Close those around it.

1181
01:18:08,768 --> 01:18:09,811
- You understand?
- Yep, got it.

1182
01:18:09,978 --> 01:18:11,271
This was meant for
one big guy, so we gotta

1183
01:18:11,354 --> 01:18:13,022
- move at the same time.
- Okay, okay. Ready.

1184
01:18:17,443 --> 01:18:18,653
We might wanna turn.

1185
01:18:18,820 --> 01:18:20,071
Turn! Turn! Turn!

1186
01:18:50,018 --> 01:18:51,519
You all right?

1187
01:18:52,562 --> 01:18:54,272
That was close.

1188
01:18:55,648 --> 01:18:56,900
I owe you one.

1189
01:18:57,400 --> 01:18:59,485
Let me just say, if aliens

1190
01:18:59,569 --> 01:19:01,321
wind up implanting eggs
in my chest or something...

1191
01:19:01,487 --> 01:19:02,614
and I eat one of you,
I'm sorry.

1192
01:19:02,780 --> 01:19:05,116
I do not want another
single pop culture reference

1193
01:19:05,199 --> 01:19:06,784
out of you for the rest
of the trip. You understand?

1194
01:19:06,868 --> 01:19:08,328
I'm trying to say
that something is coming.

1195
01:19:15,752 --> 01:19:16,836
Thanos!

1196
01:19:37,649 --> 01:19:39,651
Whoa, whoa, whoa! Please don't
put your eggs in me!

1197
01:19:41,152 --> 01:19:43,613
Stay down, clown.

1198
01:19:48,826 --> 01:19:50,912
Die, blanket of death!

1199
01:19:56,834 --> 01:19:59,754
Everybody stay where
you are. Chill the eff out.

1200
01:20:00,964 --> 01:20:02,966
I'm gonna ask you
this one time.

1201
01:20:03,716 --> 01:20:04,968
Where is Gamora?

1202
01:20:05,134 --> 01:20:07,637
Yeah. I'll do you one better.
Who's Gamora?

1203
01:20:07,929 --> 01:20:10,723
I'll do you one better.
Why is Gamora?

1204
01:20:10,890 --> 01:20:12,809
Tell me where the girl is
or I swear to you

1205
01:20:12,892 --> 01:20:14,143
I'm gonna French fry
this little freak.

1206
01:20:14,310 --> 01:20:17,146
Let's do it. You shoot my guy
and I'll blast him. Let's go!

1207
01:20:17,730 --> 01:20:20,316
Do it, Quill! I can take it.

1208
01:20:20,483 --> 01:20:22,485
- No, he can't take it!
- She's right. You can't.

1209
01:20:22,652 --> 01:20:24,696
Oh, yeah? You don't wanna tell
me where she is? That's fine.

1210
01:20:24,862 --> 01:20:25,905
I'll kill all three of you

1211
01:20:25,989 --> 01:20:27,824
and I'll beat it
out of Thanos myself.

1212
01:20:27,991 --> 01:20:28,992
Starting with you.

1213
01:20:29,075 --> 01:20:30,159
Wait, what, Thanos?

1214
01:20:30,243 --> 01:20:32,328
All right, let me ask you
this one time.

1215
01:20:32,829 --> 01:20:34,497
What master do you serve?

1216
01:20:34,664 --> 01:20:35,915
What master do I serve?

1217
01:20:35,999 --> 01:20:37,458
What am I supposed to say,
"Jesus"?

1218
01:20:38,376 --> 01:20:39,377
You're from Earth.

1219
01:20:39,460 --> 01:20:40,545
I'm not from Earth,
I'm from Missouri.

1220
01:20:40,628 --> 01:20:41,963
Yeah, that's on Earth,
dipshit.

1221
01:20:42,130 --> 01:20:43,172
What are you hassling us for?

1222
01:20:43,256 --> 01:20:45,091
So you're not
with Thanos?

1223
01:20:45,550 --> 01:20:47,385
With Thanos?

1224
01:20:47,969 --> 01:20:50,555
No, I'm here to kill Thanos.

1225
01:20:50,722 --> 01:20:52,557
He took my girl.
Wait, who are you?

1226
01:20:53,391 --> 01:20:55,101
- We're the Avengers, man.
- Oh.

1227
01:20:55,184 --> 01:20:57,478
You're the ones
Thor told us about.

1228
01:20:57,645 --> 01:20:58,813
You know Thor?

1229
01:20:58,980 --> 01:21:00,064
Yeah.

1230
01:21:00,148 --> 01:21:02,608
Tall guy, not that
good-looking, needed saving.

1231
01:21:02,775 --> 01:21:04,444
Where is he now?

1232
01:21:19,500 --> 01:21:21,377
This is the plan? We're gonna
hit him with a brick?

1233
01:21:21,544 --> 01:21:22,754
It's a mold.

1234
01:21:23,504 --> 01:21:24,505
A king's weapon.

1235
01:21:25,465 --> 01:21:27,800
Meant to be
the greatest in Asgard.

1236
01:21:28,426 --> 01:21:31,304
In theory, it could even
summon the Bifrost.

1237
01:21:31,471 --> 01:21:32,930
Did it have a name?

1238
01:21:34,182 --> 01:21:35,349
Storm breaker.

1239
01:21:35,808 --> 01:21:36,934
That's a bit much.

1240
01:21:38,978 --> 01:21:40,063
So how do we make it?

1241
01:21:41,898 --> 01:21:44,108
You'll have to restart
the forge.

1242
01:21:45,068 --> 01:21:47,278
Awaken the heart
of a dying star.

1243
01:21:49,906 --> 01:21:52,533
Rabbit, fire up the pod.

1244
01:21:56,204 --> 01:21:58,164
The hell happened
to this planet?

1245
01:21:58,331 --> 01:22:00,124
It's eight degrees
off its axis.

1246
01:22:00,208 --> 01:22:02,418
Gravitational pull
is all over the place.

1247
01:22:03,753 --> 01:22:06,547
Yeah, we got one advantage.
He's coming to us.

1248
01:22:07,507 --> 01:22:10,134
We'll use it.
All right, I have a plan.

1249
01:22:10,301 --> 01:22:11,552
Or at least
the beginnings of one.

1250
01:22:11,719 --> 01:22:13,054
It's pretty simple.
We draw him in,

1251
01:22:13,137 --> 01:22:14,347
pin him down,
get what we need.

1252
01:22:14,514 --> 01:22:16,182
Definitely don't wanna
dance with this guy.

1253
01:22:16,265 --> 01:22:17,308
We just want the gauntlet.

1254
01:22:17,892 --> 01:22:20,269
Are you yawning?

1255
01:22:20,353 --> 01:22:22,522
In the middle of this, while
I'm breaking it down? Huh?

1256
01:22:22,647 --> 01:22:23,648
Did you hear what I said?

1257
01:22:24,482 --> 01:22:26,734
I stopped listening after
you said, "We need a plan."

1258
01:22:26,901 --> 01:22:27,985
Okay, Mr. Clean
is on his own page.

1259
01:22:28,152 --> 01:22:30,988
See, "not winging it"
isn't really what they do.

1260
01:22:31,155 --> 01:22:32,657
Uh, what exactly
is it that they do?

1261
01:22:32,824 --> 01:22:34,408
Kick names, take ass.

1262
01:22:34,575 --> 01:22:35,827
Yeah, that's right.

1263
01:22:42,542 --> 01:22:43,876
All right, just get over here,
please.

1264
01:22:44,293 --> 01:22:46,212
Mr. Lord, can you get
your folks to circle up?

1265
01:22:46,379 --> 01:22:48,548
"Mr. Lord." Star-Lord is fine.

1266
01:22:51,259 --> 01:22:52,552
We gotta coalesce.

1267
01:22:52,718 --> 01:22:54,345
'Cause if all we come at him
with is a plucky attitude...

1268
01:22:54,512 --> 01:22:56,806
Dude, don't call us plucky.

1269
01:22:56,973 --> 01:22:58,141
We don't know what it means.

1270
01:22:58,558 --> 01:23:01,144
All right, we're optimistic,
yes. I like your plan.

1271
01:23:01,310 --> 01:23:03,771
Except it sucks,
so let me do the plan...

1272
01:23:03,938 --> 01:23:05,857
and that way
it might be really good.

1273
01:23:06,023 --> 01:23:07,984
Tell him about the dance-off
to save the universe.

1274
01:23:08,151 --> 01:23:10,278
- What dance-off?
- It's nothing.

1275
01:23:10,444 --> 01:23:11,487
Like in <i>Footloose,</i> the movie?

1276
01:23:11,654 --> 01:23:13,030
Exactly like <i>Footloose.</i>

1277
01:23:13,573 --> 01:23:15,074
Is it still the greatest movie
in history?

1278
01:23:15,241 --> 01:23:16,367
It never was.

1279
01:23:16,534 --> 01:23:17,577
Don't encourage this,
all right?

1280
01:23:17,660 --> 01:23:18,953
- Okay.
- We're getting no help

1281
01:23:19,036 --> 01:23:20,621
- from Flash Gordon here.
- Flash Gordon?

1282
01:23:20,705 --> 01:23:21,831
By the way,
that's a compliment.

1283
01:23:22,415 --> 01:23:23,916
Don't forget, I'm half human.

1284
01:23:24,083 --> 01:23:25,626
So that 50% of me
that's stupid...

1285
01:23:26,836 --> 01:23:27,837
that's 100% you.

1286
01:23:28,004 --> 01:23:29,255
Your math
is blowing my mind.

1287
01:23:29,338 --> 01:23:30,631
Excuse me.

1288
01:23:31,632 --> 01:23:35,052
But does your friend
often do that?

1289
01:23:36,470 --> 01:23:38,764
Strange, we all right?

1290
01:23:49,066 --> 01:23:50,109
You're back. You're all right.

1291
01:23:50,193 --> 01:23:51,986
- Hi.
- Hey, what was that?

1292
01:23:52,486 --> 01:23:56,157
I went forward in time
to view alternate futures.

1293
01:23:57,033 --> 01:23:58,576
To see all
the possible outcomes

1294
01:23:58,659 --> 01:24:00,494
of the coming conflict.

1295
01:24:01,245 --> 01:24:02,580
How many did you see?

1296
01:24:02,747 --> 01:24:04,999
14,000,605.

1297
01:24:06,667 --> 01:24:08,085
How many did we win?

1298
01:24:12,840 --> 01:24:14,008
One.

1299
01:24:35,905 --> 01:24:38,908
The stone
had better be up there.

1300
01:24:40,785 --> 01:24:42,828
For your sister's sake.

1301
01:25:03,724 --> 01:25:08,479
Welcome, Thanos, son of Alars.

1302
01:25:10,564 --> 01:25:13,818
Gamora, daughter of Thanos.

1303
01:25:13,985 --> 01:25:15,152
You know us?

1304
01:25:15,319 --> 01:25:19,865
It is my curse to know all
who journey here.

1305
01:25:20,366 --> 01:25:22,034
Where is the Soul Stone?

1306
01:25:22,743 --> 01:25:24,412
You should know...

1307
01:25:25,079 --> 01:25:28,207
it extracts a terrible price.

1308
01:25:29,542 --> 01:25:31,127
I am prepared.

1309
01:25:33,587 --> 01:25:36,007
We all think that at first.

1310
01:25:40,553 --> 01:25:42,847
We are all wrong.

1311
01:25:54,442 --> 01:25:56,777
How is it you know
this place so well?

1312
01:25:56,944 --> 01:26:01,282
A lifetime ago,
I, too, sought the stones.

1313
01:26:01,741 --> 01:26:04,452
I even held one in my hand.

1314
01:26:04,618 --> 01:26:08,664
But it cast me out,
banished me here.

1315
01:26:08,831 --> 01:26:12,877
Guiding others to a treasure
I cannot possess.

1316
01:26:21,594 --> 01:26:24,513
What you seek
lies in front of you.

1317
01:26:25,473 --> 01:26:27,600
As does what you fear.

1318
01:26:28,351 --> 01:26:29,810
What's this?

1319
01:26:30,311 --> 01:26:31,854
The price.

1320
01:26:32,021 --> 01:26:36,650
Soul holds a special place
among the Infinity Stones.

1321
01:26:37,651 --> 01:26:41,739
You might say it has
a certain wisdom.

1322
01:26:43,115 --> 01:26:44,950
Tell me what it needs.

1323
01:26:45,117 --> 01:26:48,662
To ensure that
whoever possesses it...

1324
01:26:48,829 --> 01:26:51,374
understands its power...

1325
01:26:52,333 --> 01:26:56,087
the stone demands a sacrifice.

1326
01:26:56,253 --> 01:26:57,797
Of what?

1327
01:26:58,214 --> 01:27:00,174
In order to take the stone,

1328
01:27:00,257 --> 01:27:02,676
you must lose
that which you love.

1329
01:27:05,596 --> 01:27:06,889
A soul...

1330
01:27:07,556 --> 01:27:08,808
for a soul.

1331
01:27:24,532 --> 01:27:26,867
All my life,
I dreamed of a day...

1332
01:27:27,827 --> 01:27:29,203
a moment...

1333
01:27:30,538 --> 01:27:32,623
when you got
what you deserved.

1334
01:27:34,834 --> 01:27:37,128
And I was always
so disappointed.

1335
01:27:40,714 --> 01:27:42,174
But now...

1336
01:27:46,137 --> 01:27:49,223
You kill and torture...

1337
01:27:51,183 --> 01:27:53,185
and you call it mercy.

1338
01:27:57,273 --> 01:27:59,358
The universe has judged you.

1339
01:28:00,943 --> 01:28:05,406
You asked it for a prize,
and it told you no.

1340
01:28:06,949 --> 01:28:08,451
You failed.

1341
01:28:09,827 --> 01:28:11,704
And do you wanna know why?

1342
01:28:12,663 --> 01:28:14,498
Because you love nothing.

1343
01:28:15,207 --> 01:28:16,834
No one.

1344
01:28:22,465 --> 01:28:23,632
No.

1345
01:28:28,262 --> 01:28:29,263
Really?

1346
01:28:30,306 --> 01:28:31,390
Tears?

1347
01:28:32,183 --> 01:28:34,143
They're not for him.

1348
01:28:48,407 --> 01:28:49,617
No.

1349
01:28:51,118 --> 01:28:52,536
This isn't love.

1350
01:28:53,412 --> 01:28:56,081
I ignored my destiny once.

1351
01:28:58,542 --> 01:29:00,711
I cannot do that again.

1352
01:29:01,212 --> 01:29:04,590
Even for you.

1353
01:29:28,781 --> 01:29:31,158
I'm sorry, little one.

1354
01:29:34,995 --> 01:29:36,247
No!

1355
01:31:13,844 --> 01:31:16,680
Drop to 2600, heading 0-3-0.

1356
01:31:16,847 --> 01:31:18,098
I hope you're right
about this.

1357
01:31:18,265 --> 01:31:21,143
Or we're gonna land
a lot faster than you want to.

1358
01:31:36,867 --> 01:31:38,243
When you said we were
going to open Wakanda

1359
01:31:38,327 --> 01:31:39,370
to the rest of the world...

1360
01:31:39,578 --> 01:31:41,789
this is not what I imagined.

1361
01:31:41,955 --> 01:31:43,916
And what did you imagine?

1362
01:31:44,083 --> 01:31:45,209
The Olympics.

1363
01:31:45,376 --> 01:31:47,127
Maybe even a Starbucks.

1364
01:32:01,350 --> 01:32:02,726
Should we bow?

1365
01:32:02,893 --> 01:32:04,144
Yeah, he's a king.

1366
01:32:04,478 --> 01:32:06,480
Seems like I'm always
thanking you for something.

1367
01:32:07,648 --> 01:32:09,775
What are you doing?

1368
01:32:09,858 --> 01:32:11,860
Uh, we don't do that here.

1369
01:32:12,027 --> 01:32:14,279
So how big of an assault
should we expect?

1370
01:32:14,446 --> 01:32:17,449
Uh, sir, I think you should
expect quite a big assault.

1371
01:32:17,616 --> 01:32:18,617
How we looking?

1372
01:32:18,701 --> 01:32:20,661
You will have my Kingsguard,

1373
01:32:20,744 --> 01:32:23,706
the Border Tribe,
the Dora Milaje, and...

1374
01:32:24,665 --> 01:32:27,584
And a semi-stable
100-year-old man.

1375
01:32:30,462 --> 01:32:31,630
How you been, Buck?

1376
01:32:31,797 --> 01:32:34,925
Uh, not bad,
for the end of the world.

1377
01:32:46,979 --> 01:32:48,021
Whoa.

1378
01:32:48,105 --> 01:32:50,190
The structure is polymorphic.

1379
01:32:50,649 --> 01:32:53,527
Right, we had to attach
each neuron non-sequentially.

1380
01:32:53,944 --> 01:32:55,779
Why didn't you just reprogram

1381
01:32:55,863 --> 01:32:57,990
the synapses
to work collectively?

1382
01:32:59,074 --> 01:33:02,327
Because we didn't think of it.

1383
01:33:02,745 --> 01:33:04,037
I'm sure you did your best.

1384
01:33:04,204 --> 01:33:05,414
Can you do it?

1385
01:33:06,331 --> 01:33:09,626
Yes, but there are more than
two trillion neurons here.

1386
01:33:09,793 --> 01:33:12,963
One misalignment could cause
a cascade of circuit failures.

1387
01:33:13,338 --> 01:33:14,423
It will take time, brother.

1388
01:33:16,133 --> 01:33:17,176
How long?

1389
01:33:17,259 --> 01:33:18,469
As long as you can give me.

1390
01:33:23,140 --> 01:33:25,350
Something's entered
the atmosphere.

1391
01:33:42,201 --> 01:33:44,495
Hey, Cap, we got
a situation here.

1392
01:33:54,004 --> 01:33:55,839
God, I love this place.

1393
01:33:56,006 --> 01:33:57,633
WAR MACHINE <i>Yeah,
don't start celebrating yet, guys.</i>

1394
01:33:57,716 --> 01:33:59,635
<i>We got more incoming
outside the dome.</i>

1395
01:34:18,862 --> 01:34:19,947
It's too late.

1396
01:34:20,989 --> 01:34:22,241
We need to destroy
the stone now.

1397
01:34:22,825 --> 01:34:24,451
Vision, get your ass
back on the table.

1398
01:34:24,618 --> 01:34:25,953
We will hold them off.

1399
01:34:26,119 --> 01:34:29,540
Wanda, as soon as that stone's
out of his head...

1400
01:34:29,706 --> 01:34:30,707
you blow it to hell.

1401
01:34:31,124 --> 01:34:32,209
I will.

1402
01:34:32,376 --> 01:34:35,170
Evacuate the city.
Engage all defenses.

1403
01:34:35,921 --> 01:34:37,381
And get this man a shield.

1404
01:34:47,808 --> 01:34:48,892
<i>I don't think</i>

1405
01:34:48,976 --> 01:34:50,102
<i>you get the scientifics here.</i>

1406
01:34:50,269 --> 01:34:52,729
<i>These rings are gigantic.
You wanna get them moving...</i>

1407
01:34:52,896 --> 01:34:54,273
<i>you're gonna need something
a lot bigger</i>

1408
01:34:54,356 --> 01:34:55,399
<i>to yank 'em loose.</i>

1409
01:34:55,566 --> 01:34:57,609
- Leave that to me.
- <i>Leave it to you?</i>

1410
01:34:57,776 --> 01:35:00,904
Buddy, you're in space.
All you got is a rope and a...

1411
01:35:09,329 --> 01:35:10,330
<i>Fire the engines!</i>

1412
01:35:27,890 --> 01:35:30,559
More power, rabbit!

1413
01:36:02,007 --> 01:36:03,800
Well done, boy.

1414
01:36:05,594 --> 01:36:07,512
That's Nidavellir.

1415
01:36:27,574 --> 01:36:28,575
Damn it.

1416
01:36:28,992 --> 01:36:30,535
"Damn it"? What's "damn it"?

1417
01:36:30,702 --> 01:36:32,120
<i>The mechanism
is crippled.</i>

1418
01:36:32,204 --> 01:36:33,622
- What?
- With the iris closed,

1419
01:36:33,705 --> 01:36:34,748
I can't heat the metal.

1420
01:36:34,915 --> 01:36:36,208
How long will it take
to heat it?

1421
01:36:36,667 --> 01:36:39,044
A few minutes,
maybe more. Why?

1422
01:36:41,046 --> 01:36:42,089
I'm gonna hold it open.

1423
01:36:42,255 --> 01:36:43,382
That's suicide.

1424
01:36:43,548 --> 01:36:45,968
So is facing Thanos
without that axe.

1425
01:36:55,769 --> 01:36:56,812
How we looking, Bruce?

1426
01:36:56,979 --> 01:36:58,647
Yeah, I think
I'm getting the hang of it.

1427
01:37:01,942 --> 01:37:04,027
Wow! This is amazing, man.

1428
01:37:04,111 --> 01:37:06,029
It's like being the Hulk
without actually...

1429
01:37:09,866 --> 01:37:12,077
<i>I'm okay. I'm okay.</i>

1430
01:37:13,578 --> 01:37:14,579
I've got two heat signatures

1431
01:37:14,663 --> 01:37:15,664
breaking through
the tree line.

1432
01:37:44,109 --> 01:37:46,319
Thank you
for standing with us.

1433
01:37:46,778 --> 01:37:47,779
Of course, brother.

1434
01:38:08,300 --> 01:38:09,926
Where's your other friend?

1435
01:38:10,677 --> 01:38:13,055
You will pay for his life
with yours.

1436
01:38:14,056 --> 01:38:16,224
Thanos will have that stone.

1437
01:38:17,017 --> 01:38:18,477
That's not gonna happen.

1438
01:38:18,643 --> 01:38:20,937
You are in Wakanda now.

1439
01:38:21,104 --> 01:38:24,566
Thanos will have nothing
but dust and blood.

1440
01:38:27,819 --> 01:38:29,696
We have blood to spare.

1441
01:38:41,124 --> 01:38:42,667
They surrender?

1442
01:38:43,460 --> 01:38:44,461
Not exactly.

1443
01:39:11,488 --> 01:39:12,906
What the hell?

1444
01:39:15,867 --> 01:39:17,494
Looks like we pissed her off.

1445
01:39:28,255 --> 01:39:29,798
They're killing themselves.

1446
01:40:06,042 --> 01:40:07,627
You see the teeth
on those things?

1447
01:40:07,711 --> 01:40:08,712
All right, back up, Sam.

1448
01:40:08,795 --> 01:40:10,088
You're gonna get
your wings singed.

1449
01:40:22,309 --> 01:40:23,727
<i>Cap, if these things
circle the perimeter</i>

1450
01:40:23,810 --> 01:40:24,853
<i>and get in behind us...</i>

1451
01:40:25,020 --> 01:40:26,813
<i>there's nothing
between them and Vision.</i>

1452
01:40:27,189 --> 01:40:28,940
Then we better keep 'em
in front of us.

1453
01:40:29,149 --> 01:40:30,483
How do we do that?

1454
01:40:32,861 --> 01:40:34,487
We open the barrier.

1455
01:40:36,740 --> 01:40:40,869
On my signal, open North-West
Section Seventeen.

1456
01:40:41,203 --> 01:40:43,079
<i>Requesting
confirmation, My King.</i>

1457
01:40:43,163 --> 01:40:44,831
<i>You said open the barrier?</i>

1458
01:40:44,998 --> 01:40:46,208
On my signal.

1459
01:40:46,458 --> 01:40:48,335
This will be
the end of Wakanda.

1460
01:40:49,669 --> 01:40:53,089
Then it will be
the noblest ending in history.

1461
01:41:05,936 --> 01:41:07,520
Wakanda forever!

1462
01:41:19,950 --> 01:41:20,951
Now!

1463
01:41:51,273 --> 01:41:52,691
How much longer, Shuri?

1464
01:41:52,857 --> 01:41:54,401
I've barely begun, brother.

1465
01:41:54,567 --> 01:41:56,403
You might want to pick up
the pace.

1466
01:42:03,451 --> 01:42:05,328
AIlfathers, give me strength.

1467
01:42:05,495 --> 01:42:07,289
You understand, boy?

1468
01:42:07,455 --> 01:42:10,458
You're about to take
the full force of a star.

1469
01:42:11,418 --> 01:42:12,836
It'll kill you.

1470
01:42:13,503 --> 01:42:15,714
Only if I die.

1471
01:42:16,006 --> 01:42:17,007
Yes.

1472
01:42:17,507 --> 01:42:20,260
That's what killing you means.

1473
01:42:48,246 --> 01:42:50,165
Hold it! Hold it, Thor!

1474
01:43:40,632 --> 01:43:42,592
Thor! Say something. Come on.

1475
01:43:43,510 --> 01:43:44,511
Thor, you okay?

1476
01:43:50,183 --> 01:43:51,476
I think he's dying.

1477
01:43:51,643 --> 01:43:53,603
He needs the axe!

1478
01:43:55,063 --> 01:43:56,398
Where's the handle?

1479
01:43:59,442 --> 01:44:01,778
Tree, help me find the handle!

1480
01:45:10,638 --> 01:45:12,849
There's too many of 'em!

1481
01:45:39,334 --> 01:45:42,670
You guys
are so screwed now!

1482
01:45:46,049 --> 01:45:48,051
Bring me Thanos!

1483
01:46:20,792 --> 01:46:22,293
Oh, yeah.

1484
01:46:25,421 --> 01:46:27,423
You're much more of a Thanos.

1485
01:46:29,759 --> 01:46:31,928
I take it the Maw is dead.

1486
01:46:34,222 --> 01:46:36,683
This day
extracts a heavy toll.

1487
01:46:38,393 --> 01:46:40,562
Still, he accomplished
his mission.

1488
01:46:41,020 --> 01:46:42,522
You may regret that.

1489
01:46:43,356 --> 01:46:44,732
He brought you face-to-face

1490
01:46:44,816 --> 01:46:46,234
with the Master
of the Mystic Arts.

1491
01:46:49,404 --> 01:46:51,864
And where do you think
he brought you?

1492
01:46:52,949 --> 01:46:55,660
Let me guess. Your home?

1493
01:47:00,039 --> 01:47:01,332
It was.

1494
01:47:04,085 --> 01:47:05,503
And it was beautiful.

1495
01:47:08,131 --> 01:47:10,592
Titan was like most planets.

1496
01:47:10,758 --> 01:47:13,636
Too many mouths,
not enough to go around.

1497
01:47:13,803 --> 01:47:17,056
And when we faced extinction,
I offered a solution.

1498
01:47:18,057 --> 01:47:19,267
Genocide.

1499
01:47:19,976 --> 01:47:24,063
But random, dispassionate,
fair to rich and poor alike.

1500
01:47:25,398 --> 01:47:27,567
They called me a madman.

1501
01:47:28,276 --> 01:47:30,528
And what I predicted
came to pass.

1502
01:47:33,239 --> 01:47:35,241
Congratulations,
you're a prophet.

1503
01:47:35,825 --> 01:47:37,035
I'm a survivor.

1504
01:47:37,201 --> 01:47:39,412
Who wants to murder trillions.

1505
01:47:39,579 --> 01:47:43,291
With all six stones, I could
simply snap my fingers.

1506
01:47:43,833 --> 01:47:48,546
They would all cease to exist.
I call that mercy.

1507
01:47:50,632 --> 01:47:52,133
And then what?

1508
01:47:53,468 --> 01:47:54,969
I'd finally rest...

1509
01:47:55,762 --> 01:47:58,890
and watch the sun rise
on a grateful universe.

1510
01:48:00,058 --> 01:48:03,603
The hardest choices require
the strongest wills.

1511
01:48:04,437 --> 01:48:09,150
I think you'll find our will
equal to yours.

1512
01:48:10,568 --> 01:48:11,569
Our?

1513
01:48:17,659 --> 01:48:19,077
Piece of cake, Quill.

1514
01:48:19,243 --> 01:48:21,496
Yeah, if your goal
was to piss him off.

1515
01:48:59,659 --> 01:49:00,868
Boom!

1516
01:49:01,119 --> 01:49:03,830
Don't let him close his fist.

1517
01:49:08,042 --> 01:49:09,043
Magic.

1518
01:49:09,669 --> 01:49:10,670
More magic.

1519
01:49:11,504 --> 01:49:12,505
Magic with a kick.

1520
01:49:13,131 --> 01:49:14,132
Magic with a...

1521
01:49:15,466 --> 01:49:16,759
Insect!

1522
01:49:54,172 --> 01:49:55,298
Well, well.

1523
01:49:55,465 --> 01:49:56,507
You should've killed me.

1524
01:49:56,674 --> 01:49:58,384
It would've been
a waste of parts!

1525
01:50:04,015 --> 01:50:05,141
Where's Gamora?

1526
01:50:46,474 --> 01:50:47,517
<i>Is he under?
Don't let up.</i>

1527
01:50:47,683 --> 01:50:50,311
Be quick. He is very strong.

1528
01:50:50,478 --> 01:50:52,522
Parker, help! Get over here.

1529
01:50:52,688 --> 01:50:55,024
<i>She can't hold him
much longer. Let's go.</i>

1530
01:51:00,488 --> 01:51:01,489
We gotta open
his fingers to get it off.

1531
01:51:01,656 --> 01:51:02,782
I thought you'd be
hard to catch.

1532
01:51:02,865 --> 01:51:04,075
For the record,
this was my plan.

1533
01:51:05,409 --> 01:51:07,119
You're not so strong now, huh?

1534
01:51:07,620 --> 01:51:09,372
Where is Gamora?

1535
01:51:09,455 --> 01:51:11,415
My Gamora.

1536
01:51:11,582 --> 01:51:13,626
No, bullshit!

1537
01:51:13,918 --> 01:51:15,211
Where is she?

1538
01:51:16,295 --> 01:51:17,588
He is in anguish.

1539
01:51:18,297 --> 01:51:20,299
Good.

1540
01:51:20,383 --> 01:51:22,718
He... He mourns.

1541
01:51:23,261 --> 01:51:26,889
What does
this monster have to mourn?

1542
01:51:27,598 --> 01:51:28,683
Gamora.

1543
01:51:32,562 --> 01:51:33,563
What?

1544
01:51:33,980 --> 01:51:35,481
He took her to Vormir.

1545
01:51:36,107 --> 01:51:38,067
He came back
with the Soul Stone.

1546
01:51:38,860 --> 01:51:40,361
But she didn't.

1547
01:51:42,280 --> 01:51:45,449
Okay, Quill, you gotta cool it
right now. You understand?

1548
01:51:46,325 --> 01:51:49,787
Don't, don't. Don't engage.
We almost got this off!

1549
01:51:51,038 --> 01:51:52,039
Tell me she's lying.

1550
01:51:54,500 --> 01:51:57,295
Asshole,
tell me you didn't do it!

1551
01:51:58,754 --> 01:52:02,174
I had to.

1552
01:52:02,925 --> 01:52:04,343
No, you didn't.

1553
01:52:04,427 --> 01:52:06,220
No, you didn't.

1554
01:52:10,057 --> 01:52:11,392
- No, you didn't!
- Quill!

1555
01:52:11,559 --> 01:52:13,352
Hey, stop!
Hey, stop! Stop!

1556
01:52:14,061 --> 01:52:15,062
<i>Hey, stop! Stop!</i>

1557
01:52:15,187 --> 01:52:17,023
It's coming, it's
coming. I got it, I got it!

1558
01:52:20,651 --> 01:52:21,652
Oh, God.

1559
01:53:20,127 --> 01:53:23,214
Come and get some,
space dogs!

1560
01:53:26,550 --> 01:53:29,136
Come on! Get some! Get some!

1561
01:53:29,303 --> 01:53:31,222
Come on! Get some!

1562
01:53:31,472 --> 01:53:33,516
- How much for the gun?
- Not for sale.

1563
01:53:34,141 --> 01:53:36,018
Okay. How much for the arm?

1564
01:53:37,895 --> 01:53:39,897
Oh, I'll get that arm.

1565
01:53:48,781 --> 01:53:49,782
New haircut?

1566
01:53:50,157 --> 01:53:51,450
Noticed you've copied
my beard.

1567
01:53:54,078 --> 01:53:55,830
By the way, this is
a friend of mine, Tree.

1568
01:53:56,747 --> 01:53:58,666
I am Groot.

1569
01:53:59,667 --> 01:54:01,127
I am Steve Rogers.

1570
01:54:21,188 --> 01:54:23,357
Fall back! Fall back, now!

1571
01:54:32,783 --> 01:54:34,493
Focus that fire
on the left flank, Sam.

1572
01:54:35,077 --> 01:54:36,203
I'm doing it.

1573
01:55:00,102 --> 01:55:01,729
Why was she up there
all this time?

1574
01:55:02,688 --> 01:55:05,566
She's on the field. Take it.

1575
01:55:37,181 --> 01:55:39,308
Guys, we got
a Vision situation here.

1576
01:55:42,061 --> 01:55:43,437
Somebody get to Vision!

1577
01:55:44,188 --> 01:55:45,981
<i>- I got him!</i>
- On my way.

1578
01:55:51,362 --> 01:55:54,198
He'll die alone. As will you.

1579
01:55:54,365 --> 01:55:55,658
She's not alone.

1580
01:56:21,892 --> 01:56:23,602
Oh, <i>no, you don't.</i>

1581
01:56:23,769 --> 01:56:25,229
This isn't gonna be
like New York, pal.

1582
01:56:25,396 --> 01:56:27,690
This suit's already kicked
the crap outta the Hulk.

1583
01:56:27,857 --> 01:56:28,858
<i>What? No! No!</i>

1584
01:56:32,611 --> 01:56:35,322
<i>Guys!
Vision needs backup, now!</i>

1585
01:56:37,324 --> 01:56:38,909
Hulk? Hulk,

1586
01:56:38,993 --> 01:56:40,911
I know you like making your
entrance at the last second.

1587
01:56:41,078 --> 01:56:43,706
Well, this is it, man.
This is the last, last second.

1588
01:56:48,169 --> 01:56:49,712
Hulk! Hulk!

1589
01:56:50,588 --> 01:56:51,589
Hulk!

1590
01:56:52,756 --> 01:56:54,925
No!

1591
01:56:55,092 --> 01:56:57,845
Oh, screw
you, you big, green asshole!

1592
01:56:58,012 --> 01:56:59,221
I'll do it myself!

1593
01:57:00,139 --> 01:57:01,974
<i>Come on! Yeah!</i>

1594
01:57:14,320 --> 01:57:15,905
<i>See ya!</i>

1595
01:57:27,458 --> 01:57:29,960
Hulk, we got a lot
to figure out, pal.

1596
01:57:41,013 --> 01:57:42,890
I thought you were formidable,
machine.

1597
01:57:43,849 --> 01:57:46,393
But you're dying,
like any man.

1598
01:57:54,985 --> 01:57:56,237
Get outta here!

1599
01:57:59,657 --> 01:58:00,699
Go!

1600
01:58:19,426 --> 01:58:21,095
That was really gross.

1601
01:58:48,247 --> 01:58:49,331
I thought I told you to go.

1602
01:58:50,874 --> 01:58:52,584
We don't trade lives, Captain.

1603
01:59:04,138 --> 01:59:06,181
I got you. I got you.

1604
01:59:06,432 --> 01:59:08,434
I'm sorry I can't remember
anybody's names.

1605
01:59:53,687 --> 01:59:55,189
You're full of tricks, wizard.

1606
01:59:57,274 --> 02:00:00,194
Yet you never once used
your greatest weapon.

1607
02:00:03,614 --> 02:00:04,615
A fake.

1608
02:00:12,581 --> 02:00:16,043
You throw another moon at me,
and I'm gonna lose it.

1609
02:00:16,210 --> 02:00:17,378
Stark.

1610
02:00:17,544 --> 02:00:18,629
You know me?

1611
02:00:19,254 --> 02:00:20,381
I do.

1612
02:00:20,923 --> 02:00:24,051
You're not the only one
cursed with knowledge.

1613
02:00:24,968 --> 02:00:26,303
My only curse is you.

1614
02:00:28,889 --> 02:00:29,890
Come on!

1615
02:00:57,835 --> 02:00:59,795
All that for a drop of blood.

1616
02:01:43,839 --> 02:01:45,632
You have my respect, Stark.

1617
02:01:47,301 --> 02:01:50,512
When I'm done, half of
humanity will still be alive.

1618
02:01:56,018 --> 02:01:58,103
I hope they remember you.

1619
02:02:07,905 --> 02:02:09,031
Stop.

1620
02:02:15,329 --> 02:02:16,330
Spare his life...

1621
02:02:18,123 --> 02:02:19,875
and I will give you the stone.

1622
02:02:23,420 --> 02:02:24,713
No tricks.

1623
02:02:29,510 --> 02:02:30,511
Don't.

1624
02:03:21,937 --> 02:03:23,647
One to go.

1625
02:03:33,532 --> 02:03:34,950
Where is he?

1626
02:03:43,917 --> 02:03:45,294
Did we just lose?

1627
02:03:49,214 --> 02:03:51,133
Why would you do that?

1628
02:03:54,469 --> 02:03:56,722
We're in the endgame now.

1629
02:04:21,538 --> 02:04:24,124
Are you okay?

1630
02:04:26,084 --> 02:04:27,794
What? What is it?

1631
02:04:29,963 --> 02:04:31,089
He's here.

1632
02:04:42,100 --> 02:04:45,145
Everyone, on my position.
We have incoming.

1633
02:04:47,898 --> 02:04:49,858
What the hell?

1634
02:05:15,384 --> 02:05:16,385
Cap.

1635
02:05:17,135 --> 02:05:18,595
That's him.

1636
02:05:20,639 --> 02:05:23,225
Eyes up. Stay sharp.

1637
02:05:47,708 --> 02:05:48,792
Wanda.

1638
02:05:49,835 --> 02:05:51,128
It's time.

1639
02:05:51,294 --> 02:05:52,295
No.

1640
02:05:52,462 --> 02:05:54,673
They can't stop him, Wanda,
but we can.

1641
02:05:54,840 --> 02:05:56,258
Look at me.

1642
02:05:56,425 --> 02:05:57,592
You have the power
to destroy the stone.

1643
02:05:57,676 --> 02:05:58,677
Don't.

1644
02:05:58,760 --> 02:05:59,886
You must do it. Wanda, please.

1645
02:06:01,888 --> 02:06:04,474
We are out of time.

1646
02:06:05,267 --> 02:06:06,393
I can't.

1647
02:06:06,560 --> 02:06:07,978
Yes, you can.

1648
02:06:08,645 --> 02:06:09,896
You can.

1649
02:06:11,398 --> 02:06:13,692
If he gets the stone,
half the universe dies.

1650
02:06:16,069 --> 02:06:17,571
It's not fair.

1651
02:06:18,780 --> 02:06:20,365
It shouldn't be you,
but it is.

1652
02:06:22,325 --> 02:06:23,785
It's all right.

1653
02:06:25,203 --> 02:06:26,913
You could never hurt me.

1654
02:06:35,964 --> 02:06:37,758
I just feel you.

1655
02:08:00,882 --> 02:08:02,008
It's all right.

1656
02:08:11,935 --> 02:08:13,270
It's all right.

1657
02:08:17,607 --> 02:08:18,692
I love you.

1658
02:08:48,013 --> 02:08:50,140
I understand, my child.

1659
02:08:51,683 --> 02:08:53,310
Better than anyone.

1660
02:08:54,978 --> 02:08:56,897
You could never.

1661
02:09:01,735 --> 02:09:04,738
Today, I lost more
than you can know.

1662
02:09:06,531 --> 02:09:09,159
But now is no time to mourn.

1663
02:09:11,411 --> 02:09:15,415
Now is no time at all.

1664
02:09:38,730 --> 02:09:39,731
No!

1665
02:10:37,706 --> 02:10:39,165
I told you...

1666
02:10:40,542 --> 02:10:42,377
you'd die for that.

1667
02:10:56,725 --> 02:10:58,476
You should have...

1668
02:11:01,104 --> 02:11:02,564
You should...

1669
02:11:05,066 --> 02:11:08,319
You should have
gone for the head.

1670
02:11:10,238 --> 02:11:11,239
No!

1671
02:11:44,647 --> 02:11:45,857
Daughter?

1672
02:11:53,490 --> 02:11:54,866
Did you do it?

1673
02:11:56,785 --> 02:11:57,786
Yes.

1674
02:12:06,211 --> 02:12:07,796
What did it cost?

1675
02:12:11,508 --> 02:12:13,009
Everything.

1676
02:12:23,269 --> 02:12:24,813
What did you do?

1677
02:12:26,064 --> 02:12:27,565
What'd you do?

1678
02:12:41,204 --> 02:12:42,580
Where'd he go?

1679
02:12:45,500 --> 02:12:46,584
Thor.

1680
02:12:49,879 --> 02:12:51,506
Where'd he go?

1681
02:12:51,673 --> 02:12:52,924
Steve?

1682
02:13:27,750 --> 02:13:30,044
Up, General. Up!

1683
02:13:30,628 --> 02:13:32,046
This is no place to die.

1684
02:13:47,103 --> 02:13:48,688
I am Groot.

1685
02:13:48,771 --> 02:13:50,315
Oh...

1686
02:13:51,191 --> 02:13:53,276
No, no, no!

1687
02:13:54,110 --> 02:13:56,946
Groot! No.

1688
02:14:10,376 --> 02:14:11,544
Sam!

1689
02:14:15,590 --> 02:14:17,342
Sam, where you at?

1690
02:14:26,559 --> 02:14:28,770
Something's happening.

1691
02:14:40,907 --> 02:14:42,075
Quill?

1692
02:14:49,457 --> 02:14:50,500
Steady, Quill.

1693
02:14:50,750 --> 02:14:51,918
Oh, man.

1694
02:14:56,089 --> 02:14:57,090
Tony.

1695
02:15:00,635 --> 02:15:03,096
There was no other way.

1696
02:15:08,768 --> 02:15:09,769
Mr. Stark?

1697
02:15:14,232 --> 02:15:15,566
I don't feel so good.

1698
02:15:17,652 --> 02:15:18,653
You're all right.

1699
02:15:18,736 --> 02:15:19,821
I don't... I don't know
what's happening.

1700
02:15:19,904 --> 02:15:21,447
I don't know...

1701
02:15:23,199 --> 02:15:24,284
I don't want to go.

1702
02:15:24,367 --> 02:15:26,077
I don't want to go, sir.
Please.

1703
02:15:26,244 --> 02:15:28,955
Please, I don't want to go.
I don't want to go.

1704
02:15:33,501 --> 02:15:35,003
I'm sorry.

1705
02:15:49,851 --> 02:15:51,311
He did it.

1706
02:16:16,085 --> 02:16:19,297
What is this?
What the hell is happening?

1707
02:16:36,189 --> 02:16:37,940
Oh, God.

1708
02:27:34,221 --> 02:27:35,556
<i>Still no word
from Stark?</i>

1709
02:27:35,723 --> 02:27:36,974
<i>No, not yet.</i>

1710
02:27:37,141 --> 02:27:38,434
<i>We're watching every satellite</i>

1711
02:27:38,517 --> 02:27:40,394
<i>on both hemispheres,
but still nothing.</i>

1712
02:27:40,477 --> 02:27:42,438
What is it?

1713
02:27:42,604 --> 02:27:44,940
Multiple bogeys
over Wakanda.

1714
02:27:45,107 --> 02:27:47,026
Same energy signature
as New York?

1715
02:27:47,192 --> 02:27:48,527
Ten times bigger.

1716
02:27:50,029 --> 02:27:51,155
Tell Klein
we'll meet him at...

1717
02:27:51,238 --> 02:27:52,281
Nick! Nick!

1718
02:28:05,919 --> 02:28:07,212
They okay?

1719
02:28:08,213 --> 02:28:09,965
There's no one here.

1720
02:28:19,516 --> 02:28:21,018
Call Control.

1721
02:28:21,769 --> 02:28:23,062
Code red.

1722
02:28:23,729 --> 02:28:24,730
Nick.

1723
02:28:26,398 --> 02:28:27,399
Hill.

1724
02:28:42,331 --> 02:28:43,499
Oh, no.

1725
02:28:45,125 --> 02:28:46,126
Mother...

